1
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:19,639
While we were dealing
with the rebellion issue...

2
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,399
...the infidels caught us off guard.

3
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:27,079
If you had not come in
time, Karesi Bey, many alps...

4
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:30,309
...would become martyrs, and
Karadin would become an infidel land.

5
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:34,079
What else could I do, Begum Hatun?

6
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:38,999
The infidels were attacking
the land of the Turks.

7
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:43,079
How could Karesi Bey ignore that?

8
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:46,269
Karadin is Osman Bey's property after all.

9
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:49,189
And we know about the troubles between you.

10
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:51,679
Anyone else would ignore it.

11
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,559
I am not anyone else, son.

12
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,919
I am Karesi Bey.

13
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:02,319
Osman Bey says that I work with infidels...

14
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,439
...and that I make evil plans.

15
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:09,079
Even when he speaks like that...

16
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:13,799
...and accuses me of being selfish...

17
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:17,679
...our conflict shall not overshadow
the cause of Turks.

18
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,479
Even if it's Osman Beys property...

19
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:25,519
...the lands watered with martyrs blood...

20
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,999
...are more important than anything.

21
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:33,519
Also, Osman Bey is younger than me.

22
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:37,519
Of course I will protect
the lands he can't protect...

23
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:40,879
And keep the Beys and alps he controls...

24
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:44,799
...alive.

25
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,479
Thank you, Karesi Bey.

26
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,439
Thank you.

27
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,199
Where are you going Gonca?

28
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:42,279
You disobeyed me!

29
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:44,439
You burned me, Gonca!

30
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,959
You asked for this!

31
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,959
You have nowhere to go.

32
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,319
I have no baby either.

33
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:54,319
Ever since the first time I saw you...

34
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,839
...I have been in love
with you, trickster hatun.

35
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:00,039
Only you, Alaeddin.

36
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,399
My love.

37
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,479
My test.

38
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:08,319
My homeland.

39
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:12,039
Only you, madrasah student.

40
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,319
From now on..

41
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,959
...I will just live for you.

42
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:24,679
For us.

43
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:28,559
I will cope up with everything just for you.

44
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,239
Gonca Hatun?

45
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:34,999
Gulce?

46
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,239
What are you doing here?

47
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:41,759
I came out to get some fresh
air. What are you doing here?

48
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,759
We are going to wash clothes.

49
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:46,959
Okay then.

50
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,799
I'll accompany you.

51
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,559
Come on.

52
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,559
Come on Gulce.

53
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:10,999
We haven't seen any infidels
until we arrived at the castle.

54
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:14,279
The castle wasn't in defence order either,
my Bey.

55
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,599
Alps, tell me.

56
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:31,399
An army was coming for Karadin.
Haven't you heard it?

57
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,999
We heard it, Osman.

58
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:40,119
We heard it.

59
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:47,479
We heard it, and did what was necessary.

60
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,079
Karesi Bey.

61
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,879
Karesi Bey, yeah.

62
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,419
While we were taking
precautions for The Greek rebellion...

63
00:06:57,419 --> 00:07:00,759
...that ignoble Lucas brought his army
to the castle, Osman Bey.

64
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,039
Thankfully...

65
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:10,159
...Karesi Bey saved us from a great defeat.

66
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:21,519
So Karesi Bey saved us from a big loss.

67
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,599
Tell me.

68
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,479
You have worked with the infidels...

69
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:39,879
...to plan against us each time, Karesi Bey.

70
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,439
Now you're the hero?

71
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,279
I wish to hear.

72
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,719
Karesi Bey's ship was near Bursa, my Bey.

73
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,879
He threatened Lucas to leave.

74
00:07:55,960 --> 00:08:02,439
We heard the infidels was heading
towards Osman bey's land, Karadin.

75
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:07,279
We heard Osman Bey wasn't able to fight back...

76
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:12,959
...due to the riots and uprisings in his land.

77
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:23,719
The young might not respect the elder...

78
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,039
But the elder must
protect the young at all times.

79
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:34,479
We wished to protect your land...

80
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:36,479
...which was about to be lost.

81
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:44,879
Was that a mistake Osman?

82
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:47,039
On the contrary.

83
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,839
On the contrary.

84
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,679
You did well.

85
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,479
Allah bless you.

86
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:17,759
So, you saved our Alps.

87
00:09:18,810 --> 00:09:22,479
...you protected our land.

88
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:28,119
Then..

89
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:32,319
...Karadin Castle...

90
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,799
...and the lands surroundings it...

91
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,639
..are my gift to you.

92
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:58,559
So you'll give me Karadin?

93
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,959
Certainly....

94
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,399
...we...

95
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:06,239
....will return both kindness and evil.

96
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:11,279
If you're here to be our savior...

97
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:13,399
...Allah bless you.

98
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,479
Now...

99
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,189
....in return for your favor...

100
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,239
...this castle is yours.

101
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:34,719
Osman.

102
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:39,999
I guess you want to pay me back.

103
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:48,119
You're good at both
politics and the battlefield.

104
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:50,119
You know I have many castles.

105
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:52,799
Keep Karadin.

106
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:55,719
Be my ally.

107
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,079
No.

108
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:01,799
It's against the traditions to reject gifts.

109
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,959
Karesi Bey.

110
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,879
My decision is final.

111
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,559
Begum Hatun.

112
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,439
Call back your Alps now.

113
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,479
Karadin Castle...

114
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:23,079
...is Karesi Bey's now.

115
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,679
Thank you.

116
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,519
Yusuf. Get the horses.

117
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,159
Alps.

118
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,899
Come on.

119
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:20,079
Great father...

120
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:23,239
God...

121
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:29,959
...punished me with Karadin defeat
because I made an agreement with the Turks.

122
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:35,839
But I will never kneel, father.

123
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,799
Never.

124
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:41,679
I'm going to destroy Osman.

125
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,959
Sofia?

126
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:15,279
I'll be with you while you're
destroying Osman, Lucas.

127
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:16,839
You...

128
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:19,119
How?

129
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:20,479
I thought...

130
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:24,439
You thought I died like everybody else.

131
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,359
But God...

132
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:38,359
...allowed me to live.

133
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:46,959
God brought me back so I
can pass God's wrath to him.

134
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:51,239
To end the Turks.

135
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:01,439
Together...

136
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:06,999
...we'll build a great kingdom.

137
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:16,919
A great kingdom that we will water
it's grounds with the Turk's blood.

138
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:20,679
One that feeds off death.

139
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:24,559
A hungry one.

140
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:32,559
Bloodthirsty...

141
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,919
...hungry...

142
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:39,479
...and merciless.

143
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:48,759
Is it time for revenge?

144
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:07,159
I've waited so much for this.

145
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:25,599
What did you do? What is it that I don't know?

146
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:31,359
My bey forgive me but I don't understand.

147
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:36,679
Why did we give up the castle
we got with so many sacrifices?

148
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:41,159
My Shahzade is right my bey.

149
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:44,509
We had so many fall martyr for that land.

150
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,599
My bey.

151
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,759
Forgive me but...

152
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:54,919
...didn't you say our land is the
guarantee we have for our freedom?

153
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,919
Why did we give away our land my bey?

154
00:15:57,919 --> 00:15:58,919
Beys!

155
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:01,519
Come to your senses.

156
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:06,399
We're managing a nation.

157
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,239
We...

158
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:11,199
...are taking root all over these lands.

159
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,959
Don't forget this.

160
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:15,479
The worst mistake that makes a nation fall...

161
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:19,839
...is the ignorance that is hidden under pride.

162
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,199
Tell me.

163
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,719
Don't you know Treaty of al-Hudaybiya?

164
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:28,519
Hadrath Omer and his companions...

165
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:32,359
...objected to our Prophet's call.

166
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:38,599
What did the infidels want with this treaty?

167
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:40,879
Tell me Boran.

168
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:44,719
They said Muslims won't be able to
perform umrah in Makkah, my bey.

169
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,559
See?

170
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:49,839
Why did our Prophet...

171
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:53,199
...accept this treaty which was not in favor..

172
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,759
...of Muslims?

173
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,279
Tell me Alaeddin.

174
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,639
That decision which was viewed as cruelty...

175
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:05,839
...was the key to Mecca's conquer, my bey.

176
00:17:07,839 --> 00:17:08,959
There.

177
00:17:10,598 --> 00:17:14,068
There might be evil in what
you think is good.

178
00:17:14,068 --> 00:17:17,449
There may also be good in
what you think is evil.

179
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:23,719
Of course, of course, Allah
will be the light in our road.

180
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:29,359
But do you think Karasi Bey
will rule that castle in justice?

181
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:33,639
Do you think Karadin will have peace?

182
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:39,399
Osman Bey is right. You've seen
what we couldn't see, again.

183
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:45,479
He's also protected our honor by
giving Karadin to Karasi, too.

184
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,959
Listen to me carefully now.

185
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,719
It's time for revenge now.

186
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:58,319
You'll repair everywhere, after
the rebellion in Sogut is over, Orhan.

187
00:17:58,360 --> 00:18:00,319
As you command, my Bey.

188
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:02,719
Bala.

189
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,719
Trade.

190
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:10,279
The trade of Sogut will be much better,
in fact, it will be the heart of the trade.

191
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,559
This will be your mission.

192
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:14,679
As you command, my Bey.

193
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,879
Come on, then.

194
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:23,479
Everyone back to their duty!

195
00:18:27,530 --> 00:18:30,369
Kayi Tents

196
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:39,119
Hatuns, where is Gonca, have you seen her?

197
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:47,839
Have you seen her? Where is Gonca?

198
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:52,839
What's wrong, sisters? Why don't you answer?

199
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,239
Sister.

200
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,439
What happened?

201
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,239
Fatma.

202
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:04,959
Where have you been? We were looking for
you everywhere. I thought you were gone.

203
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:10,839
I'm not going anywhere, Fatma.

204
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:15,159
Sisters were going to wash
the clothes, I was with them.

205
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:18,839
And I got rid of some stress by helping them.

206
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:27,159
They got old a lit bit but that's alright.

207
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:29,959
Then, next time take me, too.

208
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:32,159
Of course.

209
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:40,079
We were afraid for our children
because of The Greek rebellion.

210
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:44,439
Thankfully, Gonca Hatun encouraged us.

211
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:49,119
Don't be upset! Don't be afraid!
This rebellion will be over soon, too!

212
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:52,359
We've seen many fights and battles.

213
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:57,119
The ones who caused this will not be upset.
Bad things will happen to our sons again.

214
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:02,799
Come on, sisters.

215
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,999
Come on, Gulce.

216
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:31,839
Daughter, don't be upset.

217
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:52,799
Where have you been all this time?

218
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,919
It took a long time to be healed.

219
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:10,799
I've seen the death very closely.

220
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,679
I waited inside the darkness.

221
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:17,199
I made a promise.

222
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:21,359
I was going to revive for revenge.

223
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:27,599
It took a long time to gather my army,
which will drown them in their blood.

224
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,239
My soldiers!

225
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:32,959
As you see...

226
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:36,959
My wish for getting revenge
from Osman revived me.

227
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:41,159
Death became my breath.

228
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:47,199
I became the death itself.

229
00:21:56,040 --> 00:22:00,079
I won't only kill him.

230
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:10,999
I will destroy whatever Osman has in this world.

231
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,599
Sofia.

232
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:30,599
I am so glad you returned.

233
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:38,079
Our partnership...

234
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:42,039
...will be the bloodiest
alliance witnessed by history!

235
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,919
How could this happen Bayhan Bey?

236
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:58,519
How could he give the castle
we took with our swords?

237
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:02,959
Didn't we put our lives on
the line to take that castle?

238
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:06,799
Osman Bey must have a reason.

239
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:11,439
But I don't understand the reason behind it.

240
00:23:12,520 --> 00:23:15,039
It must be politics.

241
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:17,639
I don't care about politics!

242
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:20,639
Bayhan Bey, this is not good!

243
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,999
Keep in mind...

244
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:28,239
...the herd of a blind
shepherd falls from a cliff!

245
00:23:33,840 --> 00:23:36,319
Attention! Osman Bey!

246
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:59,119
Listen to me carefully now.

247
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:03,519
It's time to stop this rebellion.

248
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:08,119
The state shows its kind face sometimes...

249
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:11,279
..and when the time comes...

250
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:15,399
...it knows how to strike with its iron fist!

251
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:21,479
You will be sharper than
swords and tougher than steel.

252
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:27,759
Alaeddin.

253
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:30,199
You will go to Yenisehir.

254
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:31,839
As you command my Bey.

255
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:34,959
Orhan you will go to Sogut.

256
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:36,559
As you command my Bey.

257
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:39,919
Gencer Bey, you will
defend your property, Mekece.

258
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,079
As you command my Bey.

259
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,479
Bayhan Bey.

260
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:46,399
You are responsible for Karacahisar's defence.

261
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,079
As you command my Bey.

262
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:50,239
If anyone starts a rebellion...

263
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:54,839
...or commits crimes, you will kill them!

264
00:24:54,840 --> 00:24:56,759
As you command my Bey.

265
00:24:57,160 --> 00:25:00,399
If anyone asks for forgiveness...

266
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:03,519
...I will decide their fate.

267
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:09,039
Either victory or death!

268
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:12,999
Either victory or death!

269
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:15,399
My Bey.

270
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:31,999
My Bey, as you asked, we
conducted an investigation in Sogut.

271
00:25:32,560 --> 00:25:34,519
We caught this dog and made him talk.

272
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:38,559
The man with scarred face, he was
seen with Lucas. He started the rebellion.

273
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:44,559
Arcadeus!

274
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:49,959
Those who rule with blood..

275
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,279
...will be judged with blood.

276
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:57,319
Arcadeus, huh?

277
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,599
Every breath he takes...

278
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:02,439
...is a torment for me!

279
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:04,099
Boran.

280
00:26:04,099 --> 00:26:04,869
My Bey.

281
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:06,279
Send word to Ilbay.

282
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:08,519
I will meet him near Karakaya.

283
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,479
As you command my Bey.

284
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:12,919
Everyone get back to your duties.

285
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:31,239
You don't understand what's going on.

286
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:34,359
You are a princess, that's why.

287
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:37,519
But don't worry.

288
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:41,559
I'll tell you how life
goes on in this tribe.

289
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:45,479
What do you mean Hazal Hatun?

290
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:46,919
I don't understand.

291
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:51,039
She provoked the people
against you on the first day.

292
00:26:51,720 --> 00:26:52,479
Who?

293
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:54,279
Gonca?

294
00:26:56,680 --> 00:26:59,239
Kayi Hatuns blame you for the rebellion.

295
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:03,599
Because Gonca Hatun poisons their minds.

296
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:08,599
She is taking her baby's revenge like that.

297
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:10,399
No.

298
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,879
You don't know Gonca well.

299
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:16,439
She wouldn't do that.

300
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:48,279
Allah cursed us.

301
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:51,239
How could you do this?

302
00:27:57,320 --> 00:27:58,799
How could you?

303
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:02,039
They gave up the castle.

304
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:20,399
How could you do this?

305
00:28:25,440 --> 00:28:26,679
Beys!

306
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:28,519
Sisters!

307
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:31,679
Osman Bey ordered...

308
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:35,799
...for Karadin Castle to be owned by Karesi Bey.

309
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:42,319
It's true.

310
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:44,999
It's still Turk territory.

311
00:28:49,080 --> 00:28:50,479
Now, our part...

312
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:56,079
...is to clean up the mess
left from the uprisings.

313
00:28:57,080 --> 00:28:59,519
Sogut uprising cost a lot.

314
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,079
Our first job is..

315
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:03,399
...to revive the bazaar...

316
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:06,719
...when the uprising ends.

317
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:09,959
We'll improve Sogut Bazaar.

318
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:14,759
If Allah permits!

319
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:19,279
The bazaar will help our trade 
grow, if Allah permits.

320
00:29:19,840 --> 00:29:23,319
If Allah permits!

321
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:24,519
When Osman Bey comes...

322
00:29:25,360 --> 00:29:28,439
...he'll declare the owner of the bazaar.

323
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:20,319
You asked for me my Bey.

324
00:30:21,080 --> 00:30:22,039
Tell me.

325
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:25,039
Where's the inn of the jackal Arcadeus?

326
00:30:25,640 --> 00:30:27,159
He lives in the arena my Bey.

327
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:29,119
He trains gladiators.

328
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:31,559
He hosts feasts.

329
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:33,559
He lives and sleeps there.

330
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,159
Good.

331
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:37,559
We'll kill him in his bed.

332
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:39,679
My Bey.

333
00:30:40,600 --> 00:30:41,679
Forgive me but...

334
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:43,679
...you can't easily enter the arena.

335
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:45,679
It has one entrance.

336
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:47,679
It's loaded with soldiers.

337
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:49,679
No excuses.

338
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:54,799
Not even walls or gates can stop us.

339
00:30:58,080 --> 00:30:59,919
...will hit him in the safest place.

340
00:31:02,480 --> 00:31:03,879
As you wish my Bey.

341
00:31:07,040 --> 00:31:11,279
Brother. Arcedeus, or whatever he's called...

342
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:14,119
You said he hosts feasts.

343
00:31:14,120 --> 00:31:16,479
He likes to have fun when he can.

344
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:18,999
But he's cautious.

345
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:21,399
His most trusted men wait by the gate.

346
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:23,039
Then search everyone.

347
00:31:23,040 --> 00:31:25,039
They never let a sworded man in.

348
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:29,319
We can't fly in there.

349
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:35,529
You can't back down.
We have always..

350
00:31:35,529 --> 00:31:37,409
...kept our word.

351
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:39,579
When did we not keep it?

352
00:31:41,040 --> 00:31:42,759
We'll go inside, somehow.

353
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:45,879
Listen carefully.

354
00:32:04,800 --> 00:32:06,599
Hazal Hatun was busy.

355
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:10,599
She told Holofira Hatun that
Gonca Hatun angered the people.

356
00:32:11,520 --> 00:32:13,679
Hazal chose her side.

357
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:15,639
Let her.

358
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:20,519
Since they took the castle from me
she must be very happy right now.

359
00:32:20,520 --> 00:32:25,319
But if I'm Begum then I won't
let both Hazal and Bala be happy.

360
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:27,879
I'll get the power
I've lost back.

361
00:32:28,120 --> 00:32:31,039
May I come in Begum Hatun?

362
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:44,439
Gonca Hatun.

363
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:46,359
Welcome.

364
00:32:46,360 --> 00:32:48,159
Thank you.

365
00:32:51,680 --> 00:32:53,399
Osman Bey.

366
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:57,239
I've heard that he took Karadin Castle from you.

367
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:59,519
I wanted to see you.

368
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:02,399
Osman Bey did the right thing.

369
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:04,879
You tell me.

370
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:09,479
I've heard that the Kayi ladies
don't like the new bride here a lot.

371
00:33:09,960 --> 00:33:13,159
You can use this for your advantage.

372
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:15,159
I'm sorry?

373
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:17,879
What are you saying Begum Hatun?

374
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:21,399
The people have already
turned their backs to Holofira.

375
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:26,319
Like her being a Christian isn't enough,
that riot happened because of her too.

376
00:33:26,360 --> 00:33:28,159
So this means..

377
00:33:28,160 --> 00:33:31,759
...both you and Alaeddin have better odds now.

378
00:33:31,840 --> 00:33:34,119
Do whatever you can..

379
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:37,079
Stop there, Hatun.

380
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:39,239
I understand you.

381
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:43,079
But I have no intentions like that.

382
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:46,239
Gonca.

383
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:49,999
I'm saying this because I think of your future.

384
00:33:52,960 --> 00:33:55,319
If you don't keep your eyes peeled...

385
00:33:55,320 --> 00:33:58,839
...you'll always remain
as the wife of a Shahzade.

386
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:04,679
We're going through tough times, Begum Hatun.

387
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:08,918
I don't want the people to divide because of us.

388
00:34:09,239 --> 00:34:11,239
Excuse me.

389
00:34:18,120 --> 00:34:22,918
You'll become a wife to a bey
just with kindness and mercy huh?

390
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:28,599
Whether you want it or
not you're in war no Gonca.

391
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:36,839
Since Holofira has caused
a reaction with the people...

392
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:39,199
...use her Christianity...

393
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:43,399
...and the riot to fuel the fire.

394
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:45,799
Keep your eyes on them too.

395
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:48,319
As you wish Begum Hatun.

396
00:34:57,680 --> 00:35:02,759
You'll be the one to get burned
the worst with this fire, Bala.

397
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:07,999
I'm going to take Alaeddin who
you call your first miracle from you.

398
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:33,039
Shahzade Orhan, the murderer of the father.

399
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:35,999
Attack brothers.

400
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,239
Shahzade Orhan, killer.

401
00:35:38,240 --> 00:35:39,879
Attack brothers.

402
00:35:39,880 --> 00:35:41,319
Aykurt.

403
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:42,999
Cover all the streets.

404
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:46,159
The Greek people and the
Turks won't see each other.

405
00:35:46,160 --> 00:35:49,199
Cover the back, don't let anyone pass.

406
00:35:49,200 --> 00:35:51,079
People.

407
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:55,559
For your and your belongings' sake...

408
00:35:55,560 --> 00:35:58,679
...go to your homes right now.

409
00:35:58,680 --> 00:36:01,479
You're a murderer.

410
00:36:02,440 --> 00:36:04,759
You killed the father.

411
00:36:07,640 --> 00:36:08,999
Alps.

412
00:36:12,320 --> 00:36:14,039
Shield.

413
00:36:42,280 --> 00:36:45,519
My Shahzade, he is not an
alp and he's not one of us either.

414
00:36:45,520 --> 00:36:48,639
Lowlife. Oguz.

415
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:50,799
Oh Allah.

416
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:56,839
They're trying to egg them on.

417
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:06,399
They're giving out swords.

418
00:37:06,400 --> 00:37:08,079
Killers.

419
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:10,359
What will we do now Shahzade?

420
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:17,719
First, we'll smash the head of the snake.

421
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:26,119
Baykurt, Turan, come with me. Come on.

422
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:58,839
Trader Marco.

423
00:38:00,360 --> 00:38:02,559
Traitor Marco.

424
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:04,639
Dog Marco.

425
00:38:08,400 --> 00:38:13,559
You're taking the people, you were
sharing your bread with, to the death, huh?

426
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:18,359
Look at my face

427
00:38:19,320 --> 00:38:22,079
Orhan!

428
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:23,959
Now...

429
00:38:24,680 --> 00:38:27,959
Now, you'll suffer the consequences, Marco.

430
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:34,879
Take him.

431
00:38:35,160 --> 00:38:37,439
Get up!

432
00:38:42,240 --> 00:38:44,839
Get up, get up.

433
00:38:47,800 --> 00:38:52,439
You'll be punished for everything you did.

434
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:54,679
For everything!

435
00:38:56,120 --> 00:38:58,359
Move! Move!

436
00:39:07,040 --> 00:39:08,319
Move!

437
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:10,279
You, dog

438
00:39:14,880 --> 00:39:18,439
Move!

439
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:21,879
Move!

440
00:39:23,560 --> 00:39:24,719
Go down!

441
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:27,439
Come here.

442
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:31,439
I'm not the murderer!

443
00:39:31,880 --> 00:39:36,639
It's this traitor dog, who
led you into rebellion!

444
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:50,439
They tried everything to provoke and agitate!

445
00:39:50,720 --> 00:39:55,879
They didn't even hesitate to
kill their own religion brothers!

446
00:40:00,280 --> 00:40:02,959
My Shehzade.

447
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:08,119
This cross was with the alp, who attacked you!

448
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:14,759
Hey people! Drop your
weapons! Stop the rebellion!

449
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:34,079
From now on...

450
00:40:34,480 --> 00:40:36,399
...the state is here!

451
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:39,439
The ones who sow discord
among us have been punished!

452
00:40:40,080 --> 00:40:45,839
I swear that no one will be harmed!

453
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:49,799
But from now on..

454
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:59,519
...if there is anyone who
rebels, anyone tries to backstab...

455
00:41:02,520 --> 00:41:04,839
...he will be killed with my sword...

456
00:41:06,080 --> 00:41:08,599
...like this dog.

457
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:11,079
Never forget this.

458
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:15,919
BURSA

459
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:25,759
I'm working in Bursa Palace. Here it is.

460
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:36,959
This trades is here for the show in arena.

461
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,999
They are the guests of Commander Lukas.

462
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:44,599
Greetings to the heroic
soldiers of Commander Lukas!

463
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:46,839
Greetings!

464
00:41:47,160 --> 00:41:49,479
Send words to Arkadeus.

465
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:51,919
But...

466
00:41:52,880 --> 00:41:57,279
...if Commander Lukas learns about
this, it won't be good for you at all.

467
00:41:57,400 --> 00:41:59,319
Are you questioning their guests?

468
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:01,719
No! No! No! No! No!

469
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:05,079
They are just doing their job.

470
00:42:05,240 --> 00:42:08,639
They keep the sacred
Bursa in security? Don't they?

471
00:42:08,840 --> 00:42:10,919
Of course, they do.

472
00:42:11,520 --> 00:42:14,199
Of course, that's right.

473
00:42:14,520 --> 00:42:17,599
Petrus, commander Lucas
will not hear about this, right?

474
00:42:17,760 --> 00:42:18,759
Please forgive us.

475
00:42:18,760 --> 00:42:20,959
On the contrary.

476
00:42:21,200 --> 00:42:25,879
I will tell commander Lucas that...

477
00:42:25,880 --> 00:42:29,119
...we will have real fun with the special wine...

478
00:42:29,120 --> 00:42:32,679
...I have brought for him, and
how we will reward them.

479
00:42:39,600 --> 00:42:41,959
You deserve it.

480
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:46,279
You are embarrassing us, Petrus.

481
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:48,839
Please don't wait any longer.

482
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,759
You may pass.

483
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:52,399
Okay.

484
00:43:03,280 --> 00:43:07,239
Spread everywhere. I want to know
how many soldiers are stationed here.

485
00:43:08,120 --> 00:43:10,399
We will kill them tonight.

486
00:44:24,640 --> 00:44:27,199
What's happening here?

487
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:31,679
Come on.

488
00:44:34,240 --> 00:44:36,519
What are you doing? Come to your senses.

489
00:44:36,520 --> 00:44:38,519
What is this?

490
00:44:39,360 --> 00:44:42,799
Move.

491
00:44:42,800 --> 00:44:45,119
Stop.

492
00:44:48,560 --> 00:44:51,039
Come to your senses.

493
00:44:51,480 --> 00:44:54,999
No one will get hurt.

494
00:44:57,560 --> 00:45:00,199
Take the Turks away. Come on.

495
00:45:02,800 --> 00:45:05,199
You're brothers, don't do
this. What are you doing?

496
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:07,959
Please. What is this?

497
00:45:08,240 --> 00:45:11,159
Don't do this. Don't.

498
00:45:48,600 --> 00:45:50,319
No!

499
00:46:08,240 --> 00:46:11,199
Who is throwing the gunpowder?

500
00:46:18,120 --> 00:46:19,999
Dastards!

501
00:46:25,520 --> 00:46:27,959
Those are Arcadeus' men!

502
00:46:28,480 --> 00:46:30,279
My shahzade!

503
00:46:45,080 --> 00:46:46,639
Dastards!

504
00:46:47,000 --> 00:46:48,839
Where do you think you are running!?

505
00:46:48,840 --> 00:46:50,399
Come here!

506
00:47:31,280 --> 00:47:32,959
I have arrived, my Shahzade.

507
00:47:41,320 --> 00:47:42,559
Stay down

508
00:47:44,360 --> 00:47:46,759
You are not rusty at all, Baysungur.

509
00:47:47,080 --> 00:47:49,039
You have always been watching my back.

510
00:47:50,320 --> 00:47:51,799
Thank you.

511
00:47:52,080 --> 00:47:55,759
Killing dogs like him is
good practice, my shahzade.

512
00:47:55,920 --> 00:47:59,079
God willing, I won't get rusty
as long as Allah allows me.

513
00:47:59,120 --> 00:48:00,479
Alright.

514
00:48:00,640 --> 00:48:03,479
Now you will talk.

515
00:48:04,800 --> 00:48:07,359
-Get him up.
-Get up!

516
00:48:09,440 --> 00:48:10,999
Move!

517
00:48:12,920 --> 00:48:14,439
You will talk!

518
00:48:20,680 --> 00:48:22,319
Move!

519
00:48:25,440 --> 00:48:27,279
Enough! Shut up!

520
00:48:27,880 --> 00:48:30,039
People, listen to me!

521
00:48:30,920 --> 00:48:34,079
This dog is Arcadeus' man

522
00:48:35,120 --> 00:48:38,079
Their intention is making
Turks and Greeks fight each other!

523
00:48:38,120 --> 00:48:39,799
You are lying!

524
00:48:39,800 --> 00:48:40,879
Lies!

525
00:48:40,880 --> 00:48:41,919
Traitor Turk!

526
00:48:41,920 --> 00:48:43,639
Know that..

527
00:48:43,920 --> 00:48:46,479
...we didn't kill that priest!

528
00:48:49,400 --> 00:48:50,799
Speak!

529
00:48:51,520 --> 00:48:54,039
Speak so I will spare
your worthless life!

530
00:48:54,480 --> 00:48:55,239
Speak!

531
00:48:56,680 --> 00:48:58,559
Turks didn't kill him.

532
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:00,399
We did!

533
00:49:01,840 --> 00:49:03,639
Arcadeus did it!

534
00:49:04,440 --> 00:49:08,639
They tricked us!

535
00:49:08,920 --> 00:49:11,279
In Osman Bey's property...

536
00:49:11,440 --> 00:49:14,359
...your life and goods are in our protection.

537
00:49:15,520 --> 00:49:18,199
Everyone is free to follow their own religion.

538
00:49:18,440 --> 00:49:20,039
End this rebellion..

539
00:49:20,520 --> 00:49:22,599
...and return to your homes.

540
00:49:42,920 --> 00:49:44,519
Come on.

541
00:49:51,880 --> 00:49:53,839
Come on hatuns.

542
00:49:53,920 --> 00:49:56,599
I know you are doing your best, but...

543
00:49:56,880 --> 00:49:58,999
...we should be faster, right?

544
00:49:59,920 --> 00:50:01,879
Good day, Bala Hatun.

545
00:50:01,880 --> 00:50:04,279
Good day, Begum Hatun.

546
00:50:04,560 --> 00:50:07,959
Your carpets look pale.

547
00:50:09,160 --> 00:50:11,039
If we can help...

548
00:50:11,280 --> 00:50:13,759
Thanks, Begum Hatun.

549
00:50:14,600 --> 00:50:16,959
I'll tell you if it's necessary.

550
00:50:17,480 --> 00:50:19,039
But...

551
00:50:20,160 --> 00:50:23,399
...I wish you showed the same importance
to things that doesn't concern you...

552
00:50:23,600 --> 00:50:26,199
...to Karadiri castle.

553
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:29,759
Then the castle would still
be under your command.

554
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:33,879
And our trust in you wouldn't be shaken.

555
00:50:35,520 --> 00:50:38,399
I don't think Osman Bey
doesn't trust me anymore.

556
00:50:39,440 --> 00:50:42,599
He saw how much I cared for Karadin.

557
00:50:43,040 --> 00:50:46,559
He congratulated me on the Hatuns I assigned...

558
00:50:46,840 --> 00:50:49,119
...to keep the borders safe.

559
00:50:50,440 --> 00:50:51,719
These Hatuns..

560
00:50:53,320 --> 00:50:55,759
Are they the hatuns of your tribe?

561
00:50:55,760 --> 00:50:58,399
I assigned them to stop the uprising.

562
00:50:59,000 --> 00:51:01,359
If I hadn't, they'd have stopped Lukas.

563
00:51:01,480 --> 00:51:02,799
Hold on.

564
00:51:06,200 --> 00:51:07,919
How could you assign Hatuns...

565
00:51:08,520 --> 00:51:11,759
...without my knowledge
and without proper training...

566
00:51:11,760 --> 00:51:15,119
...prepared specially for The Sisters?

567
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:17,319
I trust them all.

568
00:51:17,520 --> 00:51:19,839
Bala Hatun they are trained.

569
00:51:20,680 --> 00:51:22,479
What's wrong with that?

570
00:51:22,480 --> 00:51:25,279
This is the state's order Begum Hatun.

571
00:51:25,640 --> 00:51:26,679
This is the state.

572
00:51:27,640 --> 00:51:30,799
What would happen if anyone was assigned?

573
00:51:31,640 --> 00:51:32,999
That is disorder.

574
00:51:33,960 --> 00:51:35,279
Peace would vanish.

575
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:39,839
You made the second mistake.

576
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:42,319
You should know that.

577
00:51:42,760 --> 00:51:45,679
First thing, you'll bring the hatuns here.

578
00:51:46,480 --> 00:51:47,999
They will be trained.

579
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:50,959
If I see them fit,
they will be assigned.

580
00:51:52,280 --> 00:51:54,399
I won't tolerate another weakness.

581
00:51:56,120 --> 00:51:56,799
Know that.

582
00:52:42,440 --> 00:52:46,479
We are the real masters of the empire.

583
00:52:47,240 --> 00:52:51,639
Eat! Drink!
Victory will be ours!

584
00:53:25,080 --> 00:53:27,159
My Bey, brother, come!

585
00:53:28,370 --> 00:53:29,359
Come.

586
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:36,719
My Bey.

587
00:53:37,400 --> 00:53:38,719
My Bey. Here.

588
00:53:39,080 --> 00:53:40,759
Here are all the keys.

589
00:53:40,760 --> 00:53:42,759
They will unlock all doors, with Allah's help.

590
00:53:42,760 --> 00:53:44,479
Alright, Cerkutay, alright.

591
00:53:44,480 --> 00:53:46,199
Come on Ibrahim. Open up.

592
00:53:52,040 --> 00:53:52,999
Here my Bey.

593
00:53:58,440 --> 00:53:59,799
Brother.

594
00:54:00,160 --> 00:54:01,479
This is water.

595
00:54:01,480 --> 00:54:04,159
What if the soldiers wanted to look inside?

596
00:54:04,160 --> 00:54:05,759
What would we do then?

597
00:54:05,760 --> 00:54:07,759
I put them in wine Boran Bey.

598
00:54:08,520 --> 00:54:11,879
I poured the wine out brothers.

599
00:54:12,360 --> 00:54:14,679
We can't dirty our holy swords with evil drinks.

600
00:54:14,680 --> 00:54:15,679
Okay.

601
00:54:15,760 --> 00:54:17,759
Okay Cerkutay.
You did well.

602
00:54:18,640 --> 00:54:19,999
Come on.

603
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:21,839
Arcedous, or whatever the name..

604
00:54:22,480 --> 00:54:24,719
He doesn't get
to live any longer.

605
00:54:24,720 --> 00:54:26,719
We'll end this tonight. Let's go.

606
00:54:35,800 --> 00:54:38,799
Kayi tribe

607
00:54:39,080 --> 00:54:42,359
The uprising was stopped in many lands.

608
00:54:43,080 --> 00:54:45,479
Thank Allah we're free of this trouble.

609
00:54:45,480 --> 00:54:46,519
Thank Allah mother.

610
00:54:46,640 --> 00:54:47,599
Thank Allah.

611
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:49,639
We stopped it, with Allah's help.

612
00:54:50,120 --> 00:54:52,879
We shut those dastards
who incited the Greek people...

613
00:54:53,600 --> 00:54:55,519
...to start the uprising.

614
00:54:58,600 --> 00:54:59,519
But...

615
00:55:00,200 --> 00:55:03,759
....Turks and Greeks were harmed.

616
00:55:04,120 --> 00:55:05,799
We must offer help.

617
00:55:07,480 --> 00:55:11,799
When we improve Sogut Market,
many people will be employed there.

618
00:55:12,120 --> 00:55:16,319
And this will heal our people faster,
if Alalh permits.

619
00:55:17,080 --> 00:55:18,399
If Allah permits, mother.

620
00:55:21,640 --> 00:55:22,679
But...

621
00:55:23,160 --> 00:55:25,559
...to ensure this never happens again...

622
00:55:26,920 --> 00:55:29,599
...it is best to harm those
who harmed us mother.

623
00:55:36,440 --> 00:55:39,839
All the places they've destroyed...

624
00:55:39,840 --> 00:55:44,799
...they should rebuild them themselves.

625
00:55:47,080 --> 00:55:49,119
Let it be a lesson.

626
00:55:56,080 --> 00:55:58,439
Gonca is right, mother Bala.

627
00:55:58,440 --> 00:56:01,599
Let those who destroyed
or even slightly caused this...

628
00:56:01,599 --> 00:56:03,959
...shall rebuild them.

629
00:56:04,880 --> 00:56:07,751
But don't let the owners
of the houses that were destroyed

630
00:56:07,751 --> 00:56:12,469
take down what's
being rebuild as a lesson...

631
00:56:18,560 --> 00:56:21,279
Both of my sister in laws are right.

632
00:56:21,280 --> 00:56:24,039
They both thought well.

633
00:56:24,760 --> 00:56:28,199
I think we should rebuild it together.

634
00:56:32,080 --> 00:56:34,079
Right.

635
00:56:34,080 --> 00:56:37,519
First us, this tribe...

636
00:56:37,960 --> 00:56:40,359
We'll be together.

637
00:56:40,360 --> 00:56:43,639
We'll dress our wounds together.

638
00:56:43,760 --> 00:56:45,879
Our pain.

639
00:56:47,320 --> 00:56:49,559
Our happiness.

640
00:56:49,680 --> 00:56:54,319
We will share them just as we share this bread.

641
00:56:57,880 --> 00:57:01,439
So that our people are united too.

642
00:57:01,680 --> 00:57:03,039
Right?

643
00:57:10,520 --> 00:57:13,119
Come on.

644
00:57:24,120 --> 00:57:26,799
Damn Turks.

645
00:57:26,920 --> 00:57:29,479
We will have fun...

646
00:57:29,480 --> 00:57:33,519
...and you will die in poverty.

647
00:57:42,880 --> 00:57:45,679
I'm going to kill you all.

648
00:57:46,040 --> 00:57:48,799
I'm going to make you beg before you die.

649
00:57:58,760 --> 00:58:01,759
You have to walk all over my dead body first.

650
00:58:07,400 --> 00:58:09,159
But...

651
00:58:10,920 --> 00:58:13,879
...you will die today.

652
00:58:14,320 --> 00:58:15,719
Osman.

653
00:58:15,720 --> 00:58:16,799
Osman, yeah.

654
00:58:16,800 --> 00:58:20,119
You won't make it out alive.

655
00:58:21,840 --> 00:58:23,239
Look here.

656
00:58:23,600 --> 00:58:26,239
You brought harm to my lands.

657
00:58:26,240 --> 00:58:28,719
You made my people turn against each other.

658
00:58:33,080 --> 00:58:34,599
Now...

659
00:58:36,800 --> 00:58:38,879
Now is the time you pay for it.

660
00:58:40,280 --> 00:58:43,359
I'm going to hang you off of my arena.

661
00:58:44,200 --> 00:58:46,359
Is that so?

662
00:58:48,640 --> 00:58:50,999
Let's see.

663
00:59:03,520 --> 00:59:05,439
Playing with a wolf...

664
00:59:06,000 --> 00:59:08,319
...ends in blood.

665
00:59:33,840 --> 00:59:35,799
Karadin..

666
00:59:35,800 --> 00:59:39,079
It will be a stain in Osman's destiny.

667
00:59:39,400 --> 00:59:43,359
And there will be no one
left who hasn't heard of this.

668
00:59:43,360 --> 00:59:46,359
Everyone is talking about this my bey.

669
00:59:46,360 --> 00:59:48,079
But I'm curious about something.

670
00:59:48,080 --> 00:59:52,119
Why did Osman give Karadin to you my bey?

671
00:59:52,360 --> 00:59:55,279
Because his honor was ruined.

672
00:59:55,600 --> 00:59:57,839
His power has lessened.

673
00:59:59,000 --> 01:00:02,759
There is no place for doubt in leadership.

674
01:00:04,160 --> 01:00:08,159
He is trying to save it but...

675
01:00:10,560 --> 01:00:13,999
...it's a meaningless effort.

676
01:00:14,280 --> 01:00:16,519
What should we do about the taxes my bey?

677
01:00:16,520 --> 01:00:20,439
Osman was getting 1/3 of what we get usually.

678
01:00:20,680 --> 01:00:22,919
Has he gone mad?

679
01:00:22,920 --> 01:00:25,039
That's not possible.

680
01:00:26,600 --> 01:00:30,519
First and foremost,
Karadin's treasury will be filled.

681
01:00:31,640 --> 01:00:33,759
Double the taxes.

682
01:00:33,760 --> 01:00:36,159
As you wish my bey.

683
01:00:46,640 --> 01:00:48,199
My Bey.

684
01:00:48,640 --> 01:00:50,759
There is an important news, my Bey.

685
01:00:51,040 --> 01:00:53,719
What is that important?

686
01:00:54,080 --> 01:00:55,479
Osman Bey.

687
01:00:55,800 --> 01:00:59,599
Osman Bey did it again, my
Bey. He suppressed the rebellion.

688
01:00:59,720 --> 01:01:03,017
They say he'll improve
the bazaar and gain...

689
01:01:03,029 --> 01:01:06,799
...income from the road
coming from China to Greeks.

690
01:01:07,840 --> 01:01:10,639
If he can improve the bazaar...

691
01:01:11,000 --> 01:01:15,399
...gold will rain in the Osman's lands.

692
01:01:15,720 --> 01:01:18,239
He'll be stronger...

693
01:01:18,800 --> 01:01:23,959
...and their people will trust Osman more.

694
01:01:24,080 --> 01:01:25,599
What should we do, my Bey?

695
01:01:25,720 --> 01:01:30,119
We'll prevent him from getting strong all alone!

696
01:01:30,400 --> 01:01:36,399
We'll take our share from
the trade in Sogut Bazaar!

697
01:01:52,720 --> 01:01:54,879
Arkadeus!

698
01:02:00,400 --> 01:02:02,039
Who did this?

699
01:02:02,880 --> 01:02:04,399
Who?

700
01:02:04,760 --> 01:02:10,879
Who dared to kill my commander in my arena?

701
01:02:16,720 --> 01:02:21,359
How did the infiltrate among you?
How did the infiltrate among you?

702
01:02:22,480 --> 01:02:23,919
How?

703
01:02:30,480 --> 01:02:32,359
Osman.

704
01:02:32,840 --> 01:02:34,479
Osman!

705
01:02:34,600 --> 01:02:36,399
I'll kill you!

706
01:02:36,480 --> 01:02:41,839
These are his last moves, you'll see.

707
01:02:46,680 --> 01:02:48,239
Soon...

708
01:02:49,600 --> 01:02:52,839
...Osman will take his place.

709
01:02:58,280 --> 01:03:00,079
Commander Lukas.

710
01:03:00,480 --> 01:03:02,119
What is it?

711
01:03:03,320 --> 01:03:05,719
Osman Bey suppressed the rebellion.

712
01:03:05,920 --> 01:03:09,999
Worse, he decided to 
revive the bazaar in Sogut.

713
01:03:10,320 --> 01:03:14,159
They say he'll improve the
bazaar and gain more income.

714
01:03:16,880 --> 01:03:18,399
How?

715
01:03:21,080 --> 01:03:22,639
How?

716
01:03:23,920 --> 01:03:27,399
How could he suppress the rebellion? How?

717
01:03:27,640 --> 01:03:30,679
So, he'll improve the bazaar.

718
01:03:32,320 --> 01:03:34,039
How nice!

719
01:03:36,600 --> 01:03:43,199
Then, I say we should
contribute to Osman's trade.

720
01:03:49,400 --> 01:03:51,439
What do you say?

721
01:03:58,440 --> 01:04:00,959
What do you have in your mind, Sofia?

722
01:04:04,960 --> 01:04:08,239
Send words to Karasi Bey, Lukas.

723
01:04:09,640 --> 01:04:12,519
I need to meet him.

724
01:04:16,840 --> 01:04:19,919
KAYI TRIBE

725
01:04:31,320 --> 01:04:34,559
Welcome, Osman Bey!

726
01:04:34,800 --> 01:04:36,999
-Thankfully, my Bey!
-Welcome!

727
01:04:47,680 --> 01:04:49,519
My Bey, welcome!

728
01:04:52,800 --> 01:04:55,919
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

729
01:05:01,960 --> 01:05:03,479
Are the missions successful?

730
01:05:03,560 --> 01:05:08,999
As you ordered, my Bey. All the rebellions
in our lands have been suppressed.

731
01:05:09,680 --> 01:05:11,239
Thank you.

732
01:05:12,640 --> 01:05:15,559
May you be live long.
May you be live long.

733
01:05:16,320 --> 01:05:17,639
Osman Bey.

734
01:05:17,840 --> 01:05:24,319
I heard you gave Karadin, for whom
my son sacrificed his life, to Karaca Bey.

735
01:05:25,080 --> 01:05:30,559
Now, it means my son died for nothing!

736
01:05:42,920 --> 01:05:44,359
Mother.

737
01:05:46,320 --> 01:05:48,839
"Do not call those
who are killed in the way of Allah...

738
01:05:49,960 --> 01:05:51,839
..."They are dead".

739
01:05:53,120 --> 01:05:54,839
On the contrary.

740
01:05:55,600 --> 01:05:57,479
Rather, they are alive." 
[2:154]

741
01:06:01,360 --> 01:06:03,439
Your son is a martyr, mother.

742
01:06:04,760 --> 01:06:07,279
Not just for Karadin castle.

743
01:06:07,800 --> 01:06:11,999
For the state, and for the
future of the true religion Islam.

744
01:06:13,240 --> 01:06:15,679
Your son gave his life.

745
01:06:17,120 --> 01:06:19,159
But his place...

746
01:06:19,920 --> 01:06:22,599
...is right next to our great prophet PBUH.

747
01:06:26,760 --> 01:06:28,199
Mother.

748
01:06:28,880 --> 01:06:30,679
Tell me.

749
01:06:32,520 --> 01:06:36,079
If I came to you and told you
that I am going for ghaza...

750
01:06:36,760 --> 01:06:40,559
...but I have no soldiers
that can hold a weapon.

751
01:06:42,880 --> 01:06:44,839
How would you answer?

752
01:06:45,960 --> 01:06:49,319
I would take up arms
and come with you!

753
01:06:55,760 --> 01:06:57,319
Thank you.

754
01:07:00,960 --> 01:07:05,519
People! Tell me. What would you do?

755
01:07:05,720 --> 01:07:11,719
We would come with you my Bey!

756
01:07:15,000 --> 01:07:17,439
Thank you.

757
01:07:19,800 --> 01:07:24,479
Since you believe me and trust me...

758
01:07:24,840 --> 01:07:26,879
...then know this.

759
01:07:27,400 --> 01:07:31,439
The reason I gave Karadin
castle to Karesi Bey is...

760
01:07:40,760 --> 01:07:42,439
...for the...

761
01:07:43,680 --> 01:07:45,959
...future of our state...

762
01:07:47,640 --> 01:07:49,599
...just as your son who sacrificed himself.

763
01:07:50,440 --> 01:07:52,359
Alright, my Bey.

764
01:07:57,720 --> 01:08:01,519
Many tried to sow discord in our lands!

765
01:08:02,000 --> 01:08:05,199
They started a rebellion after
provoking the non-Muslims!

766
01:08:05,480 --> 01:08:09,439
But we have answered them all!

767
01:08:10,720 --> 01:08:12,919
The one who lead them...

768
01:08:13,600 --> 01:08:16,118
...the tool of that dog called Lucas...

769
01:08:16,560 --> 01:08:20,919
...Arcadeus, we killed him
and hanged him on their castle!

770
01:08:21,080 --> 01:08:26,479
Long live my Bey! Long live mysBey!,

771
01:08:27,359 --> 01:08:29,999
Thanks to my Beys and my soldiers...

772
01:08:30,439 --> 01:08:32,439
...we stopped the rebellions.

773
01:08:35,279 --> 01:08:38,118
Those who sow discord lost their heads!

774
01:08:38,640 --> 01:08:41,719
Both friends and enemies saw that...

775
01:08:41,960 --> 01:08:46,238
...they cannot defeat us
with discord and treachery!

776
01:08:48,439 --> 01:08:50,359
Either victory...

777
01:08:50,880 --> 01:08:52,479
...or death!

778
01:08:52,479 --> 01:09:04,118
Either victory or death!

779
01:09:11,399 --> 01:09:16,479
The rebellion damaged the West and East
of Mekece most. Repair those areas first.

780
01:09:16,680 --> 01:09:20,359
Then you will place the
people that moved into North.

781
01:09:20,720 --> 01:09:23,799
You will bring the order back.

782
01:09:23,800 --> 01:09:25,158
As you command my Bey.

783
01:09:25,160 --> 01:09:27,639
Come on my lions!

784
01:09:28,279 --> 01:09:29,719
Someone's coming

785
01:09:36,240 --> 01:09:37,879
Let them come!

786
01:10:41,440 --> 01:10:43,159
Who are you Hatun?

787
01:10:43,400 --> 01:10:46,559
Do you have a permit to cross through my land?

788
01:10:48,280 --> 01:10:49,559
My trade documents.

789
01:10:58,480 --> 01:10:59,759
I'm Maria.

790
01:11:06,440 --> 01:11:07,559
I am a merchant.

791
01:11:08,520 --> 01:11:11,399
My trade network...

792
01:11:11,450 --> 01:11:13,269
...lies from China and Constaninople.

793
01:11:15,360 --> 01:11:17,799
So, you're here to trade.

794
01:11:20,440 --> 01:11:23,319
You heard about the bazaar
Osman Bey will set in Sogut.

795
01:11:25,160 --> 01:11:29,399
I heard about it.
But I'm not here for bazaar.

796
01:11:32,360 --> 01:11:35,959
I want to trade with you.

797
01:11:39,080 --> 01:11:40,799
I will pay you 3 times the price...

798
01:11:42,400 --> 01:11:44,479
...for all of your goods.

799
01:11:46,600 --> 01:11:48,999
Why me and not bazaar?

800
01:11:49,560 --> 01:11:53,399
Bazaar means there's a
middle man. That will slow things.

801
01:11:54,440 --> 01:11:55,879
I want to work with a supplier.

802
01:11:56,760 --> 01:12:00,799
No middle man. I'll earn more.

803
01:12:02,080 --> 01:12:03,079
...and so will he.

804
01:12:04,480 --> 01:12:08,799
Come on in then. We'll talk about your offer.

805
01:12:08,800 --> 01:12:11,279
You'll be our guest. Come.

806
01:12:12,440 --> 01:12:15,319
Carry Maria Hatun's baggage.

807
01:12:16,480 --> 01:12:19,359
Memorize all the entrances...

808
01:12:19,360 --> 01:12:22,919
...the number of soldiers
and watchers in the castle.

809
01:12:24,920 --> 01:12:27,279
Find the castle's biggest weakness.

810
01:12:27,360 --> 01:12:28,399
Don't worry.

811
01:12:29,440 --> 01:12:30,209
Here.

812
01:12:54,040 --> 01:12:55,479
I admire..

813
01:12:56,920 --> 01:13:01,239
...your everlasting ambition, Lucas.

814
01:13:02,200 --> 01:13:07,039
I stopped you getting the
castle but you still wish to talk.

815
01:13:08,840 --> 01:13:12,599
Politics can turn two friends into enemies.

816
01:13:13,040 --> 01:13:16,159
It can also turn two enemies
into friends, Karesi Bey.

817
01:13:18,280 --> 01:13:20,399
Yes you tricked me.

818
01:13:20,840 --> 01:13:25,679
But being your enemy is
bad for me right now.

819
01:13:30,640 --> 01:13:33,679
What will being your ally gain me?

820
01:13:37,080 --> 01:13:38,039
Everything.

821
01:13:42,120 --> 01:13:44,439
Osman will grow his trade.

822
01:13:45,320 --> 01:13:49,159
This won't be good for either of us.

823
01:13:55,640 --> 01:13:56,719
Right.

824
01:13:57,720 --> 01:14:00,519
I wonder what you'll say.

825
01:14:04,880 --> 01:14:08,159
I want you to give Osman a ship.

826
01:14:14,320 --> 01:14:18,159
What are you saying?
Did you lose your mind?

827
01:14:18,440 --> 01:14:20,599
You heard me Karesi Bey.

828
01:14:20,600 --> 01:14:22,599
Give him a ship.

829
01:14:23,040 --> 01:14:27,079
You'll make him take his
goods to other cities via ship.

830
01:14:27,800 --> 01:14:29,879
He'll like this offer.

831
01:14:32,200 --> 01:14:33,439
Then what?

832
01:14:35,960 --> 01:14:40,959
Then I will blow up that ship.

833
01:14:41,520 --> 01:14:44,559
All his goods will sink to the bottom.

834
01:14:46,280 --> 01:14:49,639
You have truly lost your mind.

835
01:14:52,920 --> 01:14:55,039
My ship doesn't sink.

836
01:14:56,200 --> 01:14:59,719
This will cost me a lot.

837
01:15:05,480 --> 01:15:06,639
I will pay...

838
01:15:07,520 --> 01:15:09,839
...for all the damage, Karesi Bey.

839
01:15:11,440 --> 01:15:13,199
Just give him the castle.

840
01:15:15,720 --> 01:15:17,119
Tell me.

841
01:15:18,680 --> 01:15:21,919
How will that plan go?

842
01:15:27,360 --> 01:15:30,839
Hear me people!

843
01:15:33,640 --> 01:15:36,679
Two brave men are in the battlefield.

844
01:15:36,680 --> 01:15:40,399
Both of them are braver than the other.

845
01:15:40,520 --> 01:15:45,639
A man needs to train, even if
it's training they need strength.

846
01:15:46,160 --> 01:15:48,559
The rope will be pulled...

847
01:15:48,560 --> 01:15:52,599
...and the stronger one will
knock down the weaker one.

848
01:15:52,600 --> 01:15:55,799
May Allah give you strength.

849
01:15:55,800 --> 01:15:57,599
Come on then.

850
01:15:57,800 --> 01:16:00,559
Come on Saruca, knock them down.

851
01:16:00,560 --> 01:16:03,039
Come on my lion son.

852
01:16:08,280 --> 01:16:10,399
Don't worry mother.

853
01:16:10,400 --> 01:16:12,079
I'm going to knock them down.

854
01:16:12,080 --> 01:16:15,279
We'll see who will knock down who.

855
01:16:20,240 --> 01:16:22,719
I support Turahan.

856
01:16:22,720 --> 01:16:24,679
He is stronger than all of you.

857
01:16:24,680 --> 01:16:26,239
Thank you Ghazi.

858
01:16:26,240 --> 01:16:27,879
You're hurting us Ghazi.

859
01:16:27,880 --> 01:16:30,439
Not at all, Sergeant Aykurt.

860
01:16:30,440 --> 01:16:32,079
I'm just giving my opinion.

861
01:16:32,080 --> 01:16:36,959
I even bet one gold coin
for uncle Turahan's side.

862
01:16:36,960 --> 01:16:38,579
Heavens above!

863
01:16:41,600 --> 01:16:43,519
Look at him go.

864
01:16:43,520 --> 01:16:46,399
Will you be a gambler huh?
I can't reach your ear!

865
01:16:46,400 --> 01:16:49,119
Where did you find gold?
Tell me right now.

866
01:16:52,160 --> 01:16:54,039
Ulgen Hatun.

867
01:16:55,560 --> 01:16:57,079
I gave it to him.

868
01:16:58,840 --> 01:17:02,679
Told him to go and
get cloth for clothes.

869
01:17:10,160 --> 01:17:14,359
Come on. I wish you all luck.

870
01:17:14,680 --> 01:17:15,679
Allah.

871
01:17:15,680 --> 01:17:17,079
-Oh Allah.
-Come on.

872
01:17:18,200 --> 01:17:19,359
Come on.

873
01:17:19,360 --> 01:17:21,199
Come on Saruca, come on.

874
01:17:21,200 --> 01:17:23,119
-Pull it.
-Come on.

875
01:17:23,200 --> 01:17:25,999
Come on uncle Turahan. Come on.

876
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:28,599
Come on, come on uncle Turahan.

877
01:17:28,600 --> 01:17:30,639
-Come on Saruca.
-Pull it.

878
01:17:30,640 --> 01:17:32,639
-Come on.
-Come on.

879
01:17:32,640 --> 01:17:34,199
Come on.

880
01:17:34,200 --> 01:17:35,679
-Oh Allah.
-Come on.

881
01:17:35,680 --> 01:17:37,719
-Come on.
-Come on alps.

882
01:17:39,360 --> 01:17:42,999
Oh Allah.

883
01:17:43,000 --> 01:17:44,719
Come on, unIce Turahan.

884
01:17:44,720 --> 01:17:47,959
Aykurt.
Uncle Turahan!

885
01:17:47,960 --> 01:17:50,439
Come on Sergeant Aykurt!

886
01:17:50,440 --> 01:17:52,879
-Come on.
-Oh Allah.

887
01:17:52,880 --> 01:17:55,279
-Oh Allah.
-Come on.

888
01:17:55,280 --> 01:17:57,439
Come on.

889
01:17:57,440 --> 01:17:59,199
-Come on.
-Pull it.

890
01:17:59,200 --> 01:18:01,719
-Saruca.
-Come on.

891
01:18:03,160 --> 01:18:04,199
Come on.

892
01:18:04,200 --> 01:18:05,519
My Osman.

893
01:18:06,080 --> 01:18:08,639
I've got food prepared for you.
Come, my bey.

894
01:18:08,640 --> 01:18:11,039
Thank you Bala.

895
01:18:11,560 --> 01:18:13,199
Thank you Bala.

896
01:18:13,200 --> 01:18:15,039
Thank you.

897
01:18:16,480 --> 01:18:18,119
What is it?

898
01:18:18,120 --> 01:18:20,599
What's that noise?

899
01:18:20,600 --> 01:18:24,599
To change this negative mood
and to make the people a bit happy...

900
01:18:24,600 --> 01:18:28,039
...I've told the alps to have a bit of fun.

901
01:18:29,280 --> 01:18:32,279
You thought well Bala.

902
01:18:34,000 --> 01:18:37,679
The people will of course feel better.

903
01:18:37,840 --> 01:18:39,839
But the daughter in laws...

904
01:18:39,840 --> 01:18:41,919
How will they be?

905
01:18:43,120 --> 01:18:46,999
Gonca has focused on work
to forget about her pain, my bey.

906
01:18:47,000 --> 01:18:48,759
She's okay.

907
01:18:49,160 --> 01:18:53,079
And Holofira is a new bride,
she's trying to get used to the tribe.

908
01:18:53,560 --> 01:18:57,479
She won't have a hard time
when she has you here, right dear?

909
01:19:00,280 --> 01:19:02,919
I know all sides of you, but...

910
01:19:02,920 --> 01:19:07,919
I don't know what kind of a mother in law
you are. Don't torture my daughter in laws.

911
01:19:08,200 --> 01:19:09,999
Look at this.

912
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:13,279
What are you saying as if you don't know me?

913
01:19:15,240 --> 01:19:17,039
Come on now Osman.

914
01:19:17,680 --> 01:19:20,639
I know you well.

915
01:19:20,640 --> 01:19:22,119
I do.

916
01:19:26,000 --> 01:19:28,479
Of course.

917
01:19:29,360 --> 01:19:30,599
Bala.

918
01:19:32,440 --> 01:19:35,999
You'll be their guide.

919
01:19:36,480 --> 01:19:38,079
What do they say?

920
01:19:38,680 --> 01:19:42,959
A man is the pillar of a house,
and the woman the walls.

921
01:19:44,240 --> 01:19:48,799
Now they too will be the rocks 
our sons need.

922
01:19:51,520 --> 01:19:53,679
Just as how I've raised our kids...

923
01:19:53,680 --> 01:19:55,759
...I'm going to guide them too Osman.

924
01:19:55,760 --> 01:19:57,839
Don't worry.

925
01:19:59,040 --> 01:20:01,159
Now, excuse me.

926
01:20:01,160 --> 01:20:02,999
Where are you going?

927
01:20:03,000 --> 01:20:05,199
I'm teaching The Sisters.

928
01:20:06,000 --> 01:20:10,439
If you like we can check up
on them together after you eat.

929
01:20:10,840 --> 01:20:12,919
Okay then, we'll go together.

930
01:20:12,920 --> 01:20:13,959
Okay.

931
01:20:19,160 --> 01:20:21,959
Turahan.
-Come on Saruca.

932
01:20:21,960 --> 01:20:23,799
-Come on.
-Come on.

933
01:20:23,800 --> 01:20:25,999
Turahan.
-Come on.

934
01:20:26,000 --> 01:20:28,759
-Uncle Turahan.
-Come on alps.

935
01:20:28,760 --> 01:20:30,759
Aykurt.
-Uncle Turahan.

936
01:20:30,800 --> 01:20:32,039
Come on Saruca.

937
01:20:34,040 --> 01:20:35,479
Come on!

938
01:20:36,240 --> 01:20:37,559
Come on!

939
01:20:46,560 --> 01:20:48,119
Come on!

940
01:20:52,760 --> 01:20:54,879
Come on, it's almost over!

941
01:21:00,120 --> 01:21:01,999
Come on, Sarica!

942
01:21:02,120 --> 01:21:04,959
Oh no, my son is going to lose!

943
01:21:05,640 --> 01:21:07,599
He'll bring shame on us!

944
01:21:09,040 --> 01:21:12,599
Come on now! Come on now!

945
01:21:13,400 --> 01:21:16,079
-Come on! Come on now!
-Bey!

946
01:21:16,280 --> 01:21:17,999
I can't stand!

947
01:21:18,360 --> 01:21:22,039
Sarica, I'm coming!
I'll help you, Sarica!

948
01:21:22,160 --> 01:21:24,159
-Pull!
-Stop!

949
01:21:24,320 --> 01:21:28,799
Cheating! She's cheating!

950
01:21:28,920 --> 01:21:31,159
Mother! What are you doing, mother?

951
01:21:31,560 --> 01:21:33,599
Oh Allah!

952
01:21:34,040 --> 01:21:37,039
Come on, Alps! Come on, Alps!

953
01:21:58,240 --> 01:22:02,519
You see that, Ayse? 
Look, my uncle Turan wins!

954
01:22:15,000 --> 01:22:20,319
The winner, Yusuf Bey, Turahan...

955
01:22:21,200 --> 01:22:22,679
...and Alps.

956
01:22:22,680 --> 01:22:24,559
-Oh Praise be!
-Great!

957
01:22:24,600 --> 01:22:26,959
-Oh Praise be!
-Oh Praise be!

958
01:22:27,120 --> 01:22:30,199
-Oh Praise be!
-Oh Praise be!

959
01:22:33,200 --> 01:22:37,839
Don't be upset, son. There
was injustice but you fought well.

960
01:22:38,120 --> 01:22:39,919
My lion.

961
01:22:42,440 --> 01:22:45,519
You brought shame on us and yourself.

962
01:22:51,560 --> 01:22:53,839
Don't listen to your father.

963
01:22:57,360 --> 01:22:58,799
My Bey.

964
01:23:03,000 --> 01:23:05,439
You see, Fatma Hatun?

965
01:23:05,920 --> 01:23:08,199
The weak ones lost.

966
01:23:09,960 --> 01:23:11,839
We won.

967
01:23:12,800 --> 01:23:15,119
Both sides fought well.

968
01:23:16,200 --> 01:23:19,039
But there is only one winner, of course.

969
01:23:29,120 --> 01:23:31,319
Are you okay, Sarica?

970
01:23:38,280 --> 01:23:40,239
Come on, sisters!

971
01:24:26,160 --> 01:24:30,319
All of our sister has been trained, Osman Bey.

972
01:24:30,560 --> 01:24:32,159
Bala Hatun.

973
01:24:36,320 --> 01:24:37,519
Okay.

974
01:24:37,600 --> 01:24:40,799
I've trained my
sisters personally.

975
01:24:41,120 --> 01:24:44,839
I learned this method from
a warrior coming from China.

976
01:24:44,960 --> 01:24:46,639
China, huh?

977
01:24:48,240 --> 01:24:51,799
Begum Hatun, you learned it wrong.

978
01:24:52,120 --> 01:24:55,599
They learned it from our
ancestors, from Gokturks!

979
01:24:59,200 --> 01:25:02,279
Bala, you see this?

980
01:25:03,080 --> 01:25:05,839
They lay claim to everything.

981
01:25:07,120 --> 01:25:09,199
Ours is better.

982
01:25:09,800 --> 01:25:12,879
I can train your hatuns,
too, if you wish, Bala Hatun.

983
01:25:13,000 --> 01:25:16,159
It's unnecessary, Begum Hatun.

984
01:25:16,640 --> 01:25:22,159
Then, let's see it together
if it is unnecessary or not.

985
01:25:45,120 --> 01:25:47,199
Come on Begum Hatun.

986
01:26:15,040 --> 01:26:17,799
Come on Begum Hatun, is this all you got?

987
01:26:25,680 --> 01:26:27,799
It would be rude to..

988
01:26:28,000 --> 01:26:30,679
...disarm Osman Bey's
Hatun right in front of him.

989
01:26:34,720 --> 01:26:38,359
None could disarm me until now, Begum Hatun.

990
01:27:04,960 --> 01:27:07,119
I told you Begum Hatun.

991
01:27:07,520 --> 01:27:11,039
Your fearlessness will cost you your life.

992
01:27:11,360 --> 01:27:13,079
Be more careful.

993
01:27:17,400 --> 01:27:18,799
Praise be, Bala.

994
01:27:19,000 --> 01:27:20,399
Praise be.

995
01:27:31,240 --> 01:27:33,599
You did a good job Begum Hatun.

996
01:27:34,080 --> 01:27:36,799
But The Sisters are trained well.

997
01:27:37,040 --> 01:27:38,599
No need for another method.

998
01:27:39,080 --> 01:27:39,849
Know that.

999
01:27:51,280 --> 01:27:52,039
Kismet.

1000
01:27:59,840 --> 01:28:02,239
I'm not like others, Bala.

1001
01:28:02,600 --> 01:28:03,759
I am patient.

1002
01:28:04,200 --> 01:28:07,079
I'll get to my goal even if I'm slow.

1003
01:28:12,720 --> 01:28:14,239
These are great Bayhan Bey.

1004
01:28:14,760 --> 01:28:16,639
You paid good money.

1005
01:28:16,640 --> 01:28:18,199
Where did you get these?

1006
01:28:22,080 --> 01:28:22,979
Don't touch.

1007
01:28:26,000 --> 01:28:27,729
Much of it will hurt your stomach.

1008
01:28:29,640 --> 01:28:33,719
Leave that aside now, you told
me you had an important agreement.

1009
01:28:33,720 --> 01:28:36,079
What's that?

1010
01:28:40,480 --> 01:28:43,079
It's an amazing one.

1011
01:28:43,080 --> 01:28:47,629
I'm going to make what
Begum Hatun makes in a week...

1012
01:28:47,629 --> 01:28:49,439
...in a day.

1013
01:28:49,760 --> 01:28:52,039
How will that be?

1014
01:28:52,160 --> 01:28:55,199
A Greek woman named Maria. A merchant.

1015
01:28:55,200 --> 01:28:57,319
She has amazing connections.

1016
01:28:57,320 --> 01:28:59,719
She gives supplies to caravans.

1017
01:28:59,720 --> 01:29:02,185
She doesn't mess with
the bazaar because she

1018
01:29:02,197 --> 01:29:04,839
doesn't want to give
money to the middle person.

1019
01:29:05,520 --> 01:29:08,279
She's a smart woman.

1020
01:29:08,760 --> 01:29:10,599
She is.

1021
01:29:11,000 --> 01:29:13,719
She is smart but...

1022
01:29:14,960 --> 01:29:18,559
...she is not just smart, Bayhan Bey.

1023
01:29:19,760 --> 01:29:22,039
She's very beautiful too.

1024
01:29:25,600 --> 01:29:27,559
Beautiful?

1025
01:29:32,200 --> 01:29:34,719
What kind of a woman is she?

1026
01:29:34,800 --> 01:29:36,799
Does she have a husband?

1027
01:29:36,800 --> 01:29:40,839
What is it Bayhan Bey? Why do you care if
she has a husband? What will you do with him?

1028
01:29:40,840 --> 01:29:43,319
I mean, I'm asking for...

1029
01:29:43,320 --> 01:29:46,199
Maybe we can do trade
together in the future too.

1030
01:29:46,200 --> 01:29:50,559
I mean she's smart and beautiful.
She might have a husband.

1031
01:29:50,560 --> 01:29:52,599
Or not, of course, I don't know.

1032
01:29:52,600 --> 01:29:55,319
I mean, I don't know her.

1033
01:29:57,320 --> 01:30:00,119
Who is that woman you're talking about?

1034
01:30:02,400 --> 01:30:04,279
Hatun...

1035
01:30:07,280 --> 01:30:08,759
Gencer Bey?

1036
01:30:09,600 --> 01:30:11,159
I mean...

1037
01:30:13,760 --> 01:30:15,439
What Hatun?

1038
01:30:15,840 --> 01:30:20,959
We were discussing trade with Gencer
Bey here. Weren't we, Gencer Bey?

1039
01:30:21,360 --> 01:30:22,959
We were.

1040
01:30:28,880 --> 01:30:32,279
My Bala, I told you to go easy but
you still sweated her.

1041
01:30:32,320 --> 01:30:35,399
She is still alive, she'll be thankful for that.

1042
01:30:38,040 --> 01:30:40,159
She was talking yesterday.

1043
01:30:40,760 --> 01:30:45,319
She said while you were patrolling
the borders, you praised her a lot.

1044
01:30:45,600 --> 01:30:48,279
She did her duty well, and I praised her.

1045
01:30:50,160 --> 01:30:51,199
Really?

1046
01:30:51,760 --> 01:30:57,989
Bala, she prepared the Sisters very well.
They came from every corner.

1047
01:30:57,989 --> 01:31:01,119
But Hatuns are not the same as The Sisters.

1048
01:31:01,760 --> 01:31:05,719
She got out of the rules
and I made her remember it.

1049
01:31:06,000 --> 01:31:07,399
Okay, okay.

1050
01:31:07,560 --> 01:31:11,679
If you made her remember, then it is okay.

1051
01:31:12,160 --> 01:31:13,759
Now, tell me.

1052
01:31:15,080 --> 01:31:19,239
After all that, we captured the castle, too.

1053
01:31:19,560 --> 01:31:21,279
She is ambitious.

1054
01:31:21,680 --> 01:31:26,319
She might make a mistake
with pain of her failure.

1055
01:31:26,400 --> 01:31:28,879
She showed weakness in the castle.

1056
01:31:29,000 --> 01:31:32,319
But what about trade, huh? 
The trade of Sogut.

1057
01:31:32,760 --> 01:31:37,079
Now, we need to improve Sogut's Bazaar.

1058
01:31:37,200 --> 01:31:40,439
What do you think? Can she do it?

1059
01:31:40,640 --> 01:31:41,999
Begum...

1060
01:31:43,360 --> 01:31:48,519
...with the ambition of her failure,
she'll try harder for this mission.

1061
01:31:48,760 --> 01:31:50,119
But...

1062
01:31:51,320 --> 01:31:53,719
...I want to take care of her, my Bey.

1063
01:31:53,840 --> 01:31:56,279
Of course, of course.

1064
01:31:56,640 --> 01:31:58,919
Then, let's do this way.

1065
01:31:59,440 --> 01:32:02,879
You assign her duty personally.

1066
01:32:11,840 --> 01:32:13,759
My Bey, Karasi Bey is coming.

1067
01:32:17,800 --> 01:32:19,159
Let him come.

1068
01:32:51,800 --> 01:32:53,199
Peace be with you.

1069
01:32:53,720 --> 01:32:56,599
Peace be upon you Karesi Bey.

1070
01:32:57,960 --> 01:32:59,399
Come..

1071
01:33:00,320 --> 01:33:02,719
...let's go to the tent so we can talk.

1072
01:33:05,040 --> 01:33:08,839
Your trade will vanish..

1073
01:33:08,840 --> 01:33:12,039
...just like snow in a desert, Osman.

1074
01:33:25,960 --> 01:33:27,559
Gonca Hatun.

1075
01:33:28,000 --> 01:33:30,399
Do you know why she summoned us?

1076
01:33:30,880 --> 01:33:34,479
My mother will announce whom
she gave the Sogut's management.

1077
01:33:40,400 --> 01:33:42,119
Good day.

1078
01:33:49,440 --> 01:33:53,999
From now on, Sogut bazaar's management...

1079
01:33:58,160 --> 01:34:00,639
...is under Begum Hatun.

1080
01:34:08,560 --> 01:34:09,999
Congratulations.

1081
01:34:11,680 --> 01:34:13,719
Congratulations.

1082
01:34:14,640 --> 01:34:16,999
Come on then, everyone back to work.

1083
01:34:21,240 --> 01:34:23,119
Come with me Begum Hatun.

1084
01:34:26,920 --> 01:34:29,199
The duty is yours now.

1085
01:34:31,160 --> 01:34:33,039
You feel embarrassed..

1086
01:34:33,800 --> 01:34:35,479
...because you couldn't manage...

1087
01:34:36,040 --> 01:34:38,039
...the castle.

1088
01:34:38,280 --> 01:34:39,599
I know.

1089
01:34:40,600 --> 01:34:44,359
I know you won't repeat the same mistake and...

1090
01:34:44,520 --> 01:34:47,359
...fulfill your duty in the bazaar.

1091
01:34:48,080 --> 01:34:50,719
You can be rest assured, Bala Hatun.

1092
01:35:01,400 --> 01:35:03,999
Take a seat Karesi Bey.

1093
01:35:05,320 --> 01:35:07,439
Thank you but
I haven't come to sit and chat.

1094
01:35:08,040 --> 01:35:10,319
It's been a while since yesterday.

1095
01:35:11,640 --> 01:35:15,399
I was wondering why Karesi Bey did not show up.

1096
01:35:16,520 --> 01:35:18,879
You should know that Osman..

1097
01:35:19,400 --> 01:35:22,199
...Karesi Bey wouldn't...

1098
01:35:22,480 --> 01:35:25,119
...face anyone without a reason.

1099
01:35:28,600 --> 01:35:30,159
No doubt.

1100
01:35:31,560 --> 01:35:35,799
Tell me, what's the situation
in Karadin where I gifted you.

1101
01:35:36,360 --> 01:35:38,879
Karadin that you gifted
to deny our greatness...

1102
01:35:39,480 --> 01:35:44,199
...and overshadow our help...

1103
01:35:45,200 --> 01:35:47,559
...is in a good condition, Osman Bey.

1104
01:35:48,800 --> 01:35:50,559
The situation is good.

1105
01:35:52,400 --> 01:35:53,919
Tell me.

1106
01:35:54,800 --> 01:35:57,759
What brought you...

1107
01:35:58,160 --> 01:36:00,199
...here?

1108
01:36:00,400 --> 01:36:02,039
I heard that...

1109
01:36:03,840 --> 01:36:08,079
...you want Sogut to be the biggest...

1110
01:36:08,800 --> 01:36:10,879
...bazaar in the region.

1111
01:36:11,560 --> 01:36:16,119
When I wanted to have a share in the
land trade, you destroyed the bridge...

1112
01:36:17,000 --> 01:36:20,799
...and ruined my agreement with the Byzantine.

1113
01:36:22,280 --> 01:36:26,759
So I am saying that
even if we can't be allies...

1114
01:36:27,920 --> 01:36:31,599
...let's do some business together.

1115
01:36:33,840 --> 01:36:36,239
Do you want to send caravans to Sogut?

1116
01:36:38,040 --> 01:36:41,799
But that's not enough.
To sell my goods...

1117
01:36:42,080 --> 01:36:45,839
...I want a stall in the
bazaar to sell my goods.

1118
01:36:48,120 --> 01:36:51,439
I will pay you for it.

1119
01:36:51,840 --> 01:36:54,359
If you accept...

1120
01:36:55,280 --> 01:36:58,119
...I will give you one of my ships...

1121
01:36:58,520 --> 01:37:03,279
...with its crew and captain.

1122
01:37:05,080 --> 01:37:09,039
Your goods will be sold across
the sea, all over the world...

1123
01:37:09,880 --> 01:37:13,399
...not just the bazaar in Sogut.

1124
01:37:26,560 --> 01:37:28,079
Is that so?

1125
01:37:29,320 --> 01:37:30,599
We couldn't..

1126
01:37:31,760 --> 01:37:33,159
..unite our armies.

1127
01:37:34,320 --> 01:37:35,759
We were never allies.

1128
01:37:38,600 --> 01:37:40,719
Let's unite in trade then.

1129
01:37:42,760 --> 01:37:46,039
Finally you hold the hand I raise.

1130
01:37:47,520 --> 01:37:49,839
You made the best choice.

1131
01:37:50,920 --> 01:37:53,639
Our real enemy is the infidel.

1132
01:37:54,760 --> 01:37:56,959
With this trading union...

1133
01:37:57,640 --> 01:38:00,959
...Byzantines will lose
all their money, if Allah permits.

1134
01:38:02,920 --> 01:38:03,919
Now...

1135
01:38:04,840 --> 01:38:07,679
...gather all your goods in 3 days.

1136
01:38:08,640 --> 01:38:11,039
We'll send your goods...

1137
01:38:12,440 --> 01:38:17,039
...to the provinces I agreed
to trade with via your new ship.

1138
01:38:20,920 --> 01:38:23,079
-Thank you.
-It's alright.

1139
01:38:24,480 --> 01:38:25,359
Boran.

1140
01:38:25,560 --> 01:38:26,549
My Bey.

1141
01:38:27,840 --> 01:38:28,959
Sogut.

1142
01:38:30,040 --> 01:38:31,079
The tribes.

1143
01:38:31,560 --> 01:38:33,399
Karacahisar, Mekece...

1144
01:38:35,320 --> 01:38:37,399
Send word to all the people.

1145
01:38:42,800 --> 01:38:44,359
Everyone will gather the goods.

1146
01:38:47,840 --> 01:38:49,119
As you wish my Bey.

1147
01:38:52,680 --> 01:38:55,679
Kayi Tribe.

1148
01:39:58,480 --> 01:39:59,679
May I come in my Bey?

1149
01:40:01,360 --> 01:40:02,719
Come in Orhan.

1150
01:40:10,240 --> 01:40:10,839
My Bey.

1151
01:40:12,280 --> 01:40:13,759
As you wished, my Bey.

1152
01:40:14,040 --> 01:40:16,959
The caravan left.
We're ready to head out.

1153
01:40:21,160 --> 01:40:22,639
Alright son.

1154
01:40:22,840 --> 01:40:23,879
Alright.

1155
01:40:27,040 --> 01:40:28,959
Tell me what's on your mind.

1156
01:40:31,560 --> 01:40:32,279
My Bey.

1157
01:40:33,920 --> 01:40:38,159
I never intend to question
the decision you made.

1158
01:40:38,680 --> 01:40:43,359
But I worry that Karesi might
be on to something again.

1159
01:40:46,640 --> 01:40:47,479
Look.

1160
01:40:50,400 --> 01:40:52,719
I know why you suspect him.

1161
01:40:53,880 --> 01:40:55,559
Karesi Bey might do something.

1162
01:40:56,680 --> 01:40:57,199
But...

1163
01:40:58,800 --> 01:41:01,039
...do you know what really matters?

1164
01:41:03,280 --> 01:41:05,199
The politics.

1165
01:41:09,160 --> 01:41:12,519
I made this agreement for the people.

1166
01:41:14,280 --> 01:41:15,559
What do you mean my Bey?

1167
01:41:16,720 --> 01:41:19,039
In front of the people and the Beys...

1168
01:41:19,640 --> 01:41:21,759
...we held Karesi Bey's hand.

1169
01:41:21,920 --> 01:41:24,439
We proved that...

1170
01:41:24,800 --> 01:41:27,319
We're not the ones disrupting peace.

1171
01:41:29,080 --> 01:41:33,279
So you're saying, my Bey, if
Karesi Bey makes a mistake...

1172
01:41:33,560 --> 01:41:36,519
...the people and the Beys
will make him pay for it.

1173
01:41:36,520 --> 01:41:37,879
Exactly.

1174
01:41:38,040 --> 01:41:39,319
He can set a trap.

1175
01:41:39,320 --> 01:41:41,319
He can do as he wishes.

1176
01:41:43,160 --> 01:41:44,119
Don't forget.

1177
01:41:44,800 --> 01:41:48,279
Allah is the Best of those Who sets Traps.

1178
01:41:51,040 --> 01:41:52,239
By the way...

1179
01:41:53,200 --> 01:41:54,559
...keep this up.

1180
01:41:55,360 --> 01:41:58,119
Always keep suspecting.

1181
01:41:59,120 --> 01:42:02,759
The state lives off on suspicion.

1182
01:42:03,720 --> 01:42:05,039
Yes, my Bey.

1183
01:42:09,300 --> 01:42:12,899
3 days later

1184
01:42:32,360 --> 01:42:33,959
Shame...

1185
01:42:35,320 --> 01:42:38,119
It will be a shame...

1186
01:42:41,280 --> 01:42:45,519
I've build this ship myself.

1187
01:42:45,800 --> 01:42:51,419
If what I'm going to gain
was lesser than it's worth...

1188
01:42:51,920 --> 01:42:54,279
...I wouldn't be able to do this.

1189
01:42:56,960 --> 01:42:58,759
Whatever, Sancar.

1190
01:42:58,760 --> 01:42:59,599
Yes my bey.

1191
01:42:59,840 --> 01:43:01,759
Is everything ready?

1192
01:43:01,760 --> 01:43:03,599
Yes my bey.

1193
01:43:03,600 --> 01:43:05,639
Good.

1194
01:43:06,440 --> 01:43:10,359
We'll be hitting two birds with one stone.

1195
01:43:22,880 --> 01:43:24,119
Osman.

1196
01:43:25,600 --> 01:43:28,559
Such a simple man such as you...

1197
01:43:28,560 --> 01:43:31,919
How did you dare think you can defeat me?

1198
01:43:32,400 --> 01:43:36,999
Soon enough all of your
goods will be feed for the fish.

1199
01:43:38,160 --> 01:43:41,719
Your dreams will sink to the bottom of the sea.

1200
01:43:56,360 --> 01:43:57,719
My bey.

1201
01:43:57,720 --> 01:43:59,919
Osman Bey is coming.

1202
01:44:04,960 --> 01:44:06,719
Peace be with you.

1203
01:44:06,720 --> 01:44:09,319
Peace be upon you.

1204
01:44:15,520 --> 01:44:18,199
Welcome Osman Bey.

1205
01:44:18,520 --> 01:44:20,439
Welcome.

1206
01:44:21,000 --> 01:44:23,279
Thank you Karesi Bey.

1207
01:44:23,440 --> 01:44:26,439
Welcome to you too lad.

1208
01:44:29,360 --> 01:44:34,119
My Shahzade Alaeddin told me the rest of
the goods have been loaded into the ship.

1209
01:44:34,120 --> 01:44:37,239
Now you tell me it's going to sail off, huh?

1210
01:44:38,520 --> 01:44:40,559
It's ready.

1211
01:44:40,760 --> 01:44:45,479
It's waiting for your sign to sail.

1212
01:44:45,760 --> 01:44:49,159
This ship which is the mark of our agreement...

1213
01:44:49,160 --> 01:44:52,239
...shall sail with you.

1214
01:44:59,960 --> 01:45:05,239
You had so much that is
ready to be sold off, Osman Bey.

1215
01:45:05,240 --> 01:45:07,719
This is my biggest ship.

1216
01:45:07,760 --> 01:45:10,399
Your goods wouldn't fit in
my other ships.

1217
01:45:10,400 --> 01:45:12,559
I don't like to trade small.

1218
01:45:12,560 --> 01:45:17,159
If I'm going to throw a stone then
let it be worth the pain of throwing it.

1219
01:45:17,160 --> 01:45:18,599
Yes.

1220
01:45:18,600 --> 01:45:20,599
Let it be worth it.

1221
01:45:20,600 --> 01:45:22,559
Come on then.

1222
01:45:22,560 --> 01:45:25,759
Give them the sign, Osman Bey.

1223
01:45:34,720 --> 01:45:36,959
In the name of Allah.

1224
01:45:48,960 --> 01:45:52,559
Just as those sails are filled with wind...

1225
01:45:52,560 --> 01:45:55,759
...our treasuries will be filled too.

1226
01:46:03,440 --> 01:46:05,439
How could this be?

1227
01:46:15,280 --> 01:46:17,319
Karesi Bey.

1228
01:46:17,840 --> 01:46:19,559
What is this?

1229
01:46:21,360 --> 01:46:23,119
That's it.

1230
01:46:23,120 --> 01:46:24,759
Victory is mine.

1231
01:46:24,760 --> 01:46:27,079
It always has been.

1232
01:46:27,240 --> 01:46:29,079
What is this?

1233
01:46:29,080 --> 01:46:30,839
All of our goods.

1234
01:46:30,840 --> 01:46:33,159
We loaded them all on that ship.

1235
01:46:36,840 --> 01:46:38,519
What is this?

1236
01:46:38,520 --> 01:46:41,319
All those goods, all that hard work.

1237
01:46:41,320 --> 01:46:42,719
They're all ruined now.

1238
01:46:42,720 --> 01:46:45,159
If you lost your goods...

1239
01:46:45,160 --> 01:46:47,119
...then I've lost my ship Osman.

1240
01:46:47,120 --> 01:46:49,719
That doesn't concern me.

1241
01:46:50,920 --> 01:46:53,039
You will pay for this.

1242
01:46:53,040 --> 01:46:55,719
I won't be one paying Osman.

1243
01:46:55,720 --> 01:46:58,199
I'm going to make people pay.

1244
01:47:03,480 --> 01:47:05,039
Look at me.

1245
01:47:05,040 --> 01:47:06,559
Then..

1246
01:47:06,560 --> 01:47:10,919
..you will bring me whoever
that is responsible for this.

1247
01:47:32,400 --> 01:47:33,639
Yes.

1248
01:47:34,120 --> 01:47:36,839
Let's go, Sancak. Come on

1249
01:47:37,520 --> 01:47:42,759
Let's see the booty left from Osman!

1250
01:47:43,520 --> 01:47:45,759
Let's see, my Bey, let's see.

1251
01:47:49,720 --> 01:47:52,319
You'll lose everything Osman.

1252
01:47:52,480 --> 01:47:54,679
You'll lose everything

1253
01:47:54,800 --> 01:47:58,919
I won't sleep before I finish you, Osman.

1254
01:48:00,240 --> 01:48:04,999
When we return, we'll prepare
a great celebration, Hristo.

1255
01:48:17,640 --> 01:48:20,039
Dastard!

1256
01:48:24,320 --> 01:48:26,999
Hatuns, may it be easy.

1257
01:48:29,840 --> 01:48:33,559
The caravans set out quickly thanks to you.

1258
01:48:33,760 --> 01:48:35,679
Great job.

1259
01:48:50,480 --> 01:48:51,919
May it be easy, sisters.

1260
01:48:52,040 --> 01:48:55,639
-Thank you, Gonca.
-Welcome.

1261
01:49:04,840 --> 01:49:07,039
New threads for the carpets have arrived.

1262
01:49:07,160 --> 01:49:10,279
Let's start with those together, huh?

1263
01:49:10,440 --> 01:49:14,759
Let's decorate Sogut with
our colorful carpets! Come on.

1264
01:49:14,880 --> 01:49:16,399
Come on, let's start.

1265
01:49:26,840 --> 01:49:28,679
Holofira daughter.

1266
01:49:30,000 --> 01:49:32,279
You still don't believe me, do you?

1267
01:49:32,800 --> 01:49:37,079
I told you, look! She
provokes people against you.

1268
01:49:38,600 --> 01:49:41,879
-Why would she do that?
-For his man.

1269
01:49:42,000 --> 01:49:47,399
You should take care of your husband and
make good connections with people at once.

1270
01:49:51,680 --> 01:49:53,999
It's hard when there is Gonca but..

1271
01:49:55,480 --> 01:49:57,599
Do you know her mother, Saadet?

1272
01:49:57,680 --> 01:50:02,519
I saw her once, but oh! She was disgusting!

1273
01:50:02,640 --> 01:50:05,239
She is just like her mother.

1274
01:50:06,560 --> 01:50:13,319
You don't want to cause any enmity but they
start to think badly about Orhan because of you.

1275
01:50:19,000 --> 01:50:20,919
No.

1276
01:50:21,680 --> 01:50:24,799
I can't let them harm Orhan.

1277
01:50:25,000 --> 01:50:27,559
Look, how happy they are!

1278
01:50:30,800 --> 01:50:32,239
Sisters.

1279
01:50:32,960 --> 01:50:36,279
Put what you have in your hands
down for a minute. Listen to me.

1280
01:50:36,560 --> 01:50:39,959
Why did you treat Holofira like that?

1281
01:50:40,080 --> 01:50:44,839
We don't feel like it, Gonca Hatun. She
is not one of us anyway. She is Christian.

1282
01:50:44,960 --> 01:50:47,559
And the rebellion started because of her.

1283
01:50:54,400 --> 01:50:58,039
-Don't act like this, sisters. Holofira...
-Gonca.

1284
01:51:02,280 --> 01:51:04,239
You said Holofira.

1285
01:51:04,760 --> 01:51:07,039
What were going to say about me?

1286
01:51:07,960 --> 01:51:10,199
-I told sisters...
-You...

1287
01:51:10,800 --> 01:51:13,639
...said the friendship
was over, and I said okay.

1288
01:51:13,920 --> 01:51:17,879
I thought you were in pain
but this is too much, Gonca.

1289
01:51:20,800 --> 01:51:23,759
I don't understand.
What did I do to you?

1290
01:51:23,880 --> 01:51:27,639
You deny it now? It's a shame.

1291
01:51:28,200 --> 01:51:31,359
-I can't even recoginize you anymore.
-Holofira!

1292
01:51:32,400 --> 01:51:36,199
Do you hear your words?
What did I do to you?

1293
01:51:36,800 --> 01:51:42,279
You... You blamed me for
nothing. I didn't say a word.

1294
01:51:42,520 --> 01:51:45,559
But I've understood your intention, Gonca.

1295
01:51:47,480 --> 01:51:50,639
Gonca! Holofira!

1296
01:51:52,600 --> 01:51:54,119
Come to the tent.

1297
01:52:08,240 --> 01:52:09,719
Here!

1298
01:52:10,680 --> 01:52:13,079
Osman's goods.

1299
01:52:15,320 --> 01:52:20,039
Osman lost his reputation and his goods.

1300
01:52:20,920 --> 01:52:23,599
This damaged his treasury...

1301
01:52:23,720 --> 01:52:27,279
...and the trust of his people in him, my Bey.

1302
01:52:28,040 --> 01:52:33,119
Then the only person they will trust will be me!

1303
01:52:34,360 --> 01:52:35,959
Me!

1304
01:52:37,080 --> 01:52:39,399
They think their chests are in the sea..

1305
01:52:39,400 --> 01:52:44,359
...but they will never know
that we changed the chests.

1306
01:52:45,840 --> 01:52:50,719
A Bey should always hit
two birds with one stone.

1307
01:52:54,240 --> 01:52:58,439
When the night comes, you
will load the goods to the ships.

1308
01:52:58,800 --> 01:53:00,319
As you command my Bey.

1309
01:53:01,960 --> 01:53:05,079
Open the chests.

1310
01:53:05,800 --> 01:53:09,399
Let's see how rich Osman made me.

1311
01:53:26,040 --> 01:53:29,479
My Bey, there is only stones and hay!

1312
01:53:44,080 --> 01:53:45,559
What?

1313
01:53:49,040 --> 01:53:51,519
What's going on my Bey? Where are the goods?

1314
01:54:08,200 --> 01:54:10,679
Osman!

1315
01:54:11,600 --> 01:54:13,639
Black Osman!

1316
01:54:14,840 --> 01:54:17,119
He realized everything!

1317
01:54:17,480 --> 01:54:19,839
He realized everything!

1318
01:54:42,640 --> 01:54:43,799
My Bey.

1319
01:54:45,400 --> 01:54:46,799
My Bey.

1320
01:54:48,760 --> 01:54:49,679
My Bey.

1321
01:54:49,800 --> 01:54:52,439
Yes, Cerkutay? Speak.

1322
01:54:52,880 --> 01:54:53,959
My Bey.

1323
01:54:54,560 --> 01:54:59,599
I would sacrifice a lot to
see Karesi Bey's face...

1324
01:55:00,640 --> 01:55:02,559
...when he opens the chests.

1325
01:55:02,920 --> 01:55:07,519
You should have allowed
me to sneak in and hide...

1326
01:55:07,600 --> 01:55:10,079
...and watch the shape his face takes.

1327
01:55:11,000 --> 01:55:14,759
We made great Karesi Bey
carry chests filled with stones.

1328
01:55:16,080 --> 01:55:18,479
He will never forget this lesson.

1329
01:55:19,520 --> 01:55:22,839
May brother Baysungur
long live. He did a good job.

1330
01:55:23,520 --> 01:55:25,759
That's right.

1331
01:55:26,560 --> 01:55:28,319
You were right my Bey.

1332
01:55:28,640 --> 01:55:31,279
Karesi Bey is working with that dog Lucas.

1333
01:55:31,280 --> 01:55:34,199
Their intention is to sink
our ship with the goods.

1334
01:55:34,200 --> 01:55:35,519
Are you sure?

1335
01:55:35,800 --> 01:55:38,239
I am sure,my Bey. I saw it with my own eyes.

1336
01:55:38,880 --> 01:55:42,439
Lucas' men gave Karesi Bey's alps gunpowder.

1337
01:55:42,840 --> 01:55:45,879
Alps placed the gunpowder secretly in our ship.

1338
01:55:46,160 --> 01:55:47,519
Baysungur.

1339
01:55:49,040 --> 01:55:51,759
You did a great job.

1340
01:55:52,480 --> 01:55:54,359
We will see now...

1341
01:55:54,880 --> 01:55:58,719
...whose goods will be
blown and whose ship will sink.

1342
01:56:00,440 --> 01:56:04,119
Baysungur saved our state from a great loss.

1343
01:56:05,480 --> 01:56:08,199
Long live my brave man.

1344
01:56:08,360 --> 01:56:11,559
My Bey, Alaeddin must have secured the goods.

1345
01:56:11,680 --> 01:56:14,399
The goods should wait a little longer.

1346
01:56:14,520 --> 01:56:17,319
When the time comes, we will make the caravan.

1347
01:56:18,080 --> 01:56:20,439
Now let's see...

1348
01:56:21,920 --> 01:56:25,079
...what will Baysungur learn from Lucas.

1349
01:56:25,520 --> 01:56:26,999
That's what's important.

1350
01:56:28,800 --> 01:56:29,519
Come on.

1351
01:56:37,600 --> 01:56:40,839
Karesi Bey.

1352
01:56:44,960 --> 01:56:47,319
The goods will stay here for a little longer.

1353
01:56:47,640 --> 01:56:50,479
Secure the place.
Put scouts everywhere.

1354
01:56:50,840 --> 01:56:52,959
The alps are on their places, my Bey.

1355
01:56:53,240 --> 01:56:55,239
Good, eyyAllah.

1356
01:56:56,520 --> 01:56:59,239
Come on then. We are going to the tribe.

1357
01:57:09,200 --> 01:57:10,759
Speed up!

1358
01:57:24,160 --> 01:57:27,159
What are you up to, you snake!?

1359
01:59:52,520 --> 01:59:53,799
Sofia?

1360
01:59:56,240 --> 01:59:57,399
You...

1361
01:59:59,280 --> 02:00:00,479
How?

1362
02:00:01,560 --> 02:00:03,639
How? Devil!

1363
02:00:03,640 --> 02:00:06,479
I'm no devil. I'm here to kill you.

1364
02:00:06,800 --> 02:00:09,559
Your spies are all dead.

1365
02:00:11,840 --> 02:00:16,039
I crushed your network of intelligence.

1366
02:00:21,240 --> 02:00:22,399
In Bursa..

1367
02:00:24,680 --> 02:00:26,439
...Nikea...

1368
02:00:29,520 --> 02:00:32,359
...and the rest of our cities.

1369
02:00:33,920 --> 02:00:36,479
...I killed all of your spies...

1370
02:00:38,320 --> 02:00:41,039
...that had the red tailed pigeon.

1371
02:00:49,080 --> 02:00:51,279
You're lying.

1372
02:01:13,640 --> 02:01:15,439
My brothers.

1373
02:01:17,400 --> 02:01:18,719
My brothers.

1374
02:01:19,520 --> 02:01:20,519
Now...

1375
02:01:22,280 --> 02:01:23,319
...like the rest of them...

1376
02:01:24,120 --> 02:01:26,319
...you'll die too.

1377
02:01:42,160 --> 02:01:46,399
Only Allah knows that.

1378
02:01:53,000 --> 02:01:57,399
All of you will fall by my sword one by one.

1379
02:01:57,880 --> 02:02:01,159
I'll cut out your hearts.

1380
02:02:08,960 --> 02:02:10,119
Those...

1381
02:02:11,200 --> 02:02:12,999
...who work with the devil..

1382
02:02:14,520 --> 02:02:15,559
...eventually...

1383
02:02:16,320 --> 02:02:17,919
...faces a devil.

1384
02:02:27,000 --> 02:02:27,999
Devil.

1385
02:02:36,080 --> 02:02:38,279
Come here. Come here.

1386
02:02:54,560 --> 02:02:56,479
It won't be that easy.

1387
02:02:58,240 --> 02:03:01,199
Allah. In the name of Allah.

1388
02:03:11,480 --> 02:03:13,639
Allah.

1389
02:03:28,560 --> 02:03:31,399
Take him to Osman.

1390
02:03:38,040 --> 02:03:40,719
He'll take his last breath next to him.

1391
02:03:43,320 --> 02:03:44,199
Take him.

1392
02:03:54,480 --> 02:03:56,919
All of your spies are dead Osman.

1393
02:03:58,240 --> 02:04:02,639
After this much damage,
you'll only dream of conquest.

1394
02:04:10,120 --> 02:04:11,959
Tell me what's happening?

1395
02:04:12,040 --> 02:04:15,799
What's happening that you
fight in front of the people?

1396
02:04:15,800 --> 02:04:19,359
I don't know mother.
You have to ask Holofira.

1397
02:04:19,680 --> 02:04:21,999
She is the one who caused it out of nowhere.

1398
02:04:22,000 --> 02:04:25,279
So you don't know huh?
Did you start to lie too Gonca?

1399
02:04:25,280 --> 02:04:26,719
Hatun.

1400
02:04:26,720 --> 02:04:28,079
Come to your senses.

1401
02:04:28,080 --> 02:04:31,799
You've been provoking the people against
me ever since the day I came to the tribe.

1402
02:04:31,800 --> 02:04:32,919
What?

1403
02:04:32,920 --> 02:04:34,759
What does that mean girl?

1404
02:04:34,760 --> 02:04:36,159
Mother!

1405
02:04:36,560 --> 02:04:38,879
The people turned their back to me.

1406
02:04:38,880 --> 02:04:40,959
Just because I'm a Christian.

1407
02:04:40,960 --> 02:04:43,759
They hold me responsible for the Greek riot too.

1408
02:04:44,280 --> 02:04:48,119
Since Gonca is mad at me she
is provoking them against me.

1409
02:04:48,120 --> 02:04:49,399
Holofira.

1410
02:04:49,400 --> 02:04:52,439
Hear what you're saying.

1411
02:04:53,440 --> 02:04:55,519
Is this true Gonca?

1412
02:04:56,000 --> 02:04:57,519
Mother?

1413
02:04:57,880 --> 02:04:59,999
Do you believe this?

1414
02:05:00,000 --> 02:05:01,679
I didn't believe it either.

1415
02:05:01,680 --> 02:05:03,719
But I saw it.

1416
02:05:04,200 --> 02:05:05,999
You are...

1417
02:05:06,920 --> 02:05:09,599
...just as bad as
your ill-souled mother.

1418
02:05:09,800 --> 02:05:11,439
Holofira.

1419
02:05:13,560 --> 02:05:15,319
Mother.

1420
02:05:15,480 --> 02:05:17,159
Do you think so?

1421
02:05:17,160 --> 02:05:19,879
No, there's something wrong. It's clear.

1422
02:05:20,440 --> 02:05:21,999
Listen to me well.

1423
02:05:22,000 --> 02:05:23,319
Holofira.

1424
02:05:23,320 --> 02:05:25,799
I'll take care of the people.

1425
02:05:25,800 --> 02:05:29,519
But I don't want anything akin to
what happened today to happen again.

1426
02:05:29,520 --> 02:05:30,999
Come to your senses.

1427
02:05:31,000 --> 02:05:33,279
You are Kayi's daughters in law.

1428
02:05:33,280 --> 02:05:35,159
People are watching you.

1429
02:05:35,160 --> 02:05:39,759
Not just them. The enemies
who want to defeat us, destroy us.

1430
02:05:40,160 --> 02:05:43,319
You are the first people they will go to.

1431
02:05:43,480 --> 02:05:46,279
My sons are the wings of this nation.

1432
02:05:46,680 --> 02:05:49,959
And you, the supporters of those wings.

1433
02:05:50,040 --> 02:05:51,559
From now on..

1434
02:05:51,560 --> 02:05:53,479
...you will act accordingly.

1435
02:05:53,480 --> 02:05:56,399
I don't want to see any
mistakes from both of you.

1436
02:06:01,720 --> 02:06:05,639
The first thing those who
wish to hurt this nation...

1437
02:06:06,240 --> 02:06:08,839
...will do is to rip it's wings.

1438
02:06:08,840 --> 02:06:10,719
But as long as I'm alive...

1439
02:06:10,720 --> 02:06:13,159
...I will never let that happen.

1440
02:06:18,760 --> 02:06:21,719
How...

1441
02:06:21,920 --> 02:06:22,959
How...

1442
02:06:22,960 --> 02:06:24,839
How did he know?

1443
02:06:24,840 --> 02:06:26,759
Where are Osman's goods?

1444
02:06:26,760 --> 02:06:29,679
Osman Bey sent chests
filled with stones and hay.

1445
02:06:29,680 --> 02:06:32,559
We don't know where he placed the goods.

1446
02:06:36,720 --> 02:06:39,159
Osman.

1447
02:06:39,920 --> 02:06:43,279
Are you taking out your anger Lucas?

1448
02:06:44,920 --> 02:06:48,879
Osman emptied all of his goods out. All of them.

1449
02:06:49,360 --> 02:06:50,599
Karesi.

1450
02:06:50,600 --> 02:06:54,079
We gave him gold for nothing.

1451
02:06:54,440 --> 02:06:55,879
I swear...

1452
02:06:55,920 --> 02:07:01,119
...he will pay the price he
made me pay with his blood.

1453
02:07:01,880 --> 02:07:04,279
Calm down.

1454
02:07:04,800 --> 02:07:07,399
We are the strong ones.

1455
02:07:08,640 --> 02:07:14,199
Losing gold is not a problem
if it helps us to eliminate Osman.

1456
02:07:21,520 --> 02:07:25,039
I've sent him a gift he won't forget.

1457
02:07:26,920 --> 02:07:29,999
He'll be receiving it any moment now.

1458
02:07:30,720 --> 02:07:31,999
What?

1459
02:07:32,680 --> 02:07:36,439
I've cut Osman's arteries.

1460
02:07:36,720 --> 02:07:39,799
I've destroyed his network from
which he gathered information.

1461
02:07:40,920 --> 02:07:43,319
A bey that has...

1462
02:07:43,480 --> 02:07:46,799
...no eyes or ears...

1463
02:07:46,920 --> 02:07:48,399
...anywhere.

1464
02:07:51,000 --> 02:07:53,839
What can he do now?

1465
02:07:54,160 --> 02:07:55,839
You...

1466
02:07:56,200 --> 02:07:57,079
You...

1467
02:07:57,080 --> 02:07:57,479
You..

1468
02:07:58,000 --> 02:07:59,919
You're a genius.

1469
02:07:59,920 --> 02:08:01,239
Sofia.

1470
02:08:02,480 --> 02:08:04,719
Osman Bey is coming.

1471
02:08:04,720 --> 02:08:07,079
-Welcome my bey.
-Osman Bey.

1472
02:08:07,080 --> 02:08:09,559
-Welcome Bey.
-Welcome my bey.

1473
02:08:09,560 --> 02:08:12,519
May Allah give you a long life my bey.

1474
02:08:12,520 --> 02:08:14,519
-Welcome my bey.
-Welcome.

1475
02:08:16,720 --> 02:08:18,519
Welcome Osman Bey.

1476
02:08:25,680 --> 02:08:27,559
Osman Bey.

1477
02:08:28,200 --> 02:08:32,999
Did the ship that's carrying
our goods sail safe and sound?

1478
02:08:33,760 --> 02:08:35,919
When it departed...

1479
02:08:36,280 --> 02:08:39,439
..they shot the ship with
The Greek Fire and sunk it.

1480
02:08:39,440 --> 02:08:41,359
What? Did the ship sink?

1481
02:08:41,360 --> 02:08:43,119
All of our hard work gone to waste...

1482
02:08:43,120 --> 02:08:46,279
Who is the one that has done this Osman Bey?

1483
02:08:46,800 --> 02:08:51,479
The ones who always harmed us
all this time.

1484
02:08:51,960 --> 02:08:53,319
But...

1485
02:08:53,320 --> 02:08:58,359
...we knew about our enemy's plans
beforehand and took every precaution.

1486
02:08:58,360 --> 02:09:00,159
Don't worry.

1487
02:09:00,160 --> 02:09:02,399
All of the goods are safe.

1488
02:09:03,840 --> 02:09:06,799
What has sunk to the bottom of that sea...

1489
02:09:07,320 --> 02:09:09,679
...is our enemyâ€™s nerve.

1490
02:09:09,680 --> 02:09:20,479
-Long live Osman bey.
-Long live Osman Bey.

1491
02:09:21,840 --> 02:09:23,599
Long live Osman Bey.

1492
02:09:26,280 --> 02:09:28,199
Someone's coming.

1493
02:09:29,880 --> 02:09:31,719
Is that Baysungur?

1494
02:09:32,400 --> 02:09:35,319
Baysungur is coming. He is injured.

1495
02:09:35,920 --> 02:09:37,839
Baysungur...

1496
02:09:40,200 --> 02:09:41,839
Who did this?

1497
02:09:41,840 --> 02:09:43,799
Let me go, I'll go to my bey.

1498
02:09:43,800 --> 02:09:46,839
Let me go, I'll go to my bey.

1499
02:09:46,840 --> 02:09:48,519
Who did this Baysungur?

1500
02:09:48,520 --> 02:09:50,079
Hurry up, come on!

1501
02:09:50,080 --> 02:09:52,559
Make way.

1502
02:10:06,800 --> 02:10:08,119
How could it be, my Bey?

1503
02:10:08,600 --> 02:10:09,959
Baysungur.

1504
02:10:10,640 --> 02:10:12,159
Baysungur!

1505
02:10:13,840 --> 02:10:15,879
Baysungur! Baysungur!

1506
02:10:29,600 --> 02:10:32,079
-Baysungur!
-My brother!

1507
02:10:34,480 --> 02:10:35,719
Baysungur!

1508
02:10:35,800 --> 02:10:39,119
Come on. Come here, my warrior.

1509
02:10:39,480 --> 02:10:41,519
What is this?

1510
02:10:42,160 --> 02:10:45,519
-Baysungur! Baysungur!

1511
02:10:49,600 --> 02:10:51,079
Baysungur.

1512
02:10:54,440 --> 02:10:56,519
Who did this, huh?

1513
02:10:56,760 --> 02:11:00,199
Tell me, my warrior, who
did this? Who did this to you?

1514
02:11:00,560 --> 02:11:04,879
My time has come, my Bey.

1515
02:11:05,800 --> 02:11:08,639
Don't talk like that. Don't
talk like that, Baysungur.

1516
02:11:08,760 --> 02:11:16,039
Brother, don't do it! No! No! No!
You're not going! You are not leaving!

1517
02:11:16,360 --> 02:11:18,519
Baysungur, my lion brother.

1518
02:11:18,600 --> 02:11:21,079
No! Hang on! Hang on!

1519
02:11:21,120 --> 02:11:24,959
Come on, we are going to
the healing tent! Alps! Help me!

1520
02:11:25,080 --> 02:11:27,599
Baysungur, hang on.

1521
02:11:33,080 --> 02:11:35,559
I'm going to The Righteous, my Bey.

1522
02:11:43,200 --> 02:11:44,239
My Bey.

1523
02:11:46,440 --> 02:11:47,959
The box, my Bey.

1524
02:11:55,400 --> 02:11:58,039
Wait, hang on!
Hang on! Baysungur!

1525
02:12:22,520 --> 02:12:24,799
Our spies...

1526
02:12:27,000 --> 02:12:31,479
They martyred them my Bey!

1527
02:12:42,920 --> 02:12:47,239
May our state last forever.

1528
02:12:52,040 --> 02:12:53,959
May...

1529
02:12:55,280 --> 02:12:56,719
May...

1530
02:12:57,320 --> 02:12:59,879
May a thousand...

1531
02:13:01,520 --> 02:13:03,919
...Baysungurs...

1532
02:13:04,440 --> 02:13:06,319
...sacrifice themselves for you.

1533
02:13:07,080 --> 02:13:08,759
Who did this?

1534
02:13:09,160 --> 02:13:13,119
Who did this? Lukas? Karasi Bey?

1535
02:13:13,200 --> 02:13:16,719
Tell me. Who did this to you?

1536
02:13:20,760 --> 02:13:22,279
Who did this?

1537
02:13:27,400 --> 02:13:28,519
Sop...

1538
02:13:29,320 --> 02:13:32,639
Tell me! Who did this?

1539
02:13:34,120 --> 02:13:39,599
I bear witness that there is none
worthy of worship except Allah...

1540
02:13:39,760 --> 02:13:41,479
Don't do it, brother.

1541
02:13:42,360 --> 02:13:49,159
...and I bear witness that
Mohammad is His servant...

1542
02:13:52,600 --> 02:13:54,719
..and messenger.

1543
02:14:03,240 --> 02:14:05,119
Baysungur!

1544
02:14:07,520 --> 02:14:09,799
My lion brother!

1545
02:14:10,040 --> 02:14:11,919
Baysungur!

1546
02:14:42,000 --> 02:14:45,679
Indeed, we belong to Allah, and
Indeed, to Him, we shall return.

1547
02:15:01,320 --> 02:15:02,959
My warrior.

1548
02:15:05,000 --> 02:15:07,239
Don't you worry.

1549
02:15:08,040 --> 02:15:09,679
I'll take your revenge.

1550
02:15:10,560 --> 02:15:15,839
I swear, the people who
did this to you will pay dearly!

1551
02:15:17,680 --> 02:15:20,479
I am going to kill them all! All of them!